window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1"]={"id":"CGL-22-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1","title":"CGL 22 OCT 2026 SHIFT 1","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000071581","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"Choose the option that has the same relationship with the third term as the second term has with the first.<br><b>SRH : 42 :: RCB : ?</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जिसका तीसरे पद के साथ वही संबंध है जो दूसरे पद का पहले पद के साथ है।<br><b>SRH : 42 :: RCB : ?</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"19"},"2":{"en":"20"},"3":{"en":"23"},"4":{"en":"24"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Position of the letters in the alphabet:<br>S = 19, R = 18, H = 8 → 19 + 18 + 8 = 45<br>45 − 3 (number of letters) = 42<br>Similarly, R = 18, C = 3, B = 2 → 18 + 3 + 2 = 23<br>23 − 3 = 20<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 20.</b>","hi":"वर्णमाला में अक्षरों का स्थान:<br>S = 19, R = 18, H = 8 → 19 + 18 + 8 = 45<br>45 − 3 (अक्षरों की संख्या) = 42<br>उसी प्रकार, R = 18, C = 3, B = 2 → 18 + 3 + 2 = 23<br>23 − 3 = 20<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 20 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000071582","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Which number doesn’t belong: 17, 19, 23, 27, 29, 31 [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सी संख्या इस समूह की नहीं है: 17, 19, 23, 27, 29, 31 [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"17"},"2":{"en":"19"},"3":{"en":"23"},"4":{"en":"27"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"17, 19, 23, 29 and 31 are all prime numbers, i.e. each of them is divisible only by 1 and itself.<br>27 = 3 × 3 × 3, so it is divisible by 3 and 9 as well; hence it is not a prime number.<br>Therefore 27 does not belong to the group.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 27.</b>","hi":"17, 19, 23, 29 और 31 सभी अभाज्य संख्याएँ हैं, अर्थात् ये केवल 1 और स्वयं से विभाज्य हैं।<br>27 = 3 × 3 × 3, अतः यह 3 और 9 से भी विभाज्य है; इसलिए यह अभाज्य संख्या नहीं है।<br>इसलिए 27 इस समूह का नहीं है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 27 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000071583","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"If WATER = 67 and EARTH = 52, then ELEMENT = ? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि WATER = 67 तथा EARTH = 52 है, तो ELEMENT = ? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"64"},"2":{"en":"54"},"3":{"en":"74"},"4":{"en":"72"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The code is the sum of the alphabetical positions of the letters.<br>WATER → W(23) + A(1) + T(20) + E(5) + R(18) = 67 ✓<br>EARTH → E(5) + A(1) + R(18) + T(20) + H(8) = 52 ✓<br>ELEMENT → E(5) + L(12) + E(5) + M(13) + E(5) + N(14) + T(20) = 74<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 74.</b>","hi":"कोड अक्षरों के वर्णमाला-स्थानों का योग है।<br>WATER → W(23) + A(1) + T(20) + E(5) + R(18) = 67 ✓<br>EARTH → E(5) + A(1) + R(18) + T(20) + H(8) = 52 ✓<br>ELEMENT → E(5) + L(12) + E(5) + M(13) + E(5) + N(14) + T(20) = 74<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 74 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000071584","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Complete the series.<br><b>100, 95, 190, 185, 370, ?</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"श्रृंखला पूरी कीजिए।<br><b>100, 95, 190, 185, 370, ?</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"365"},"2":{"en":"360"},"3":{"en":"375"},"4":{"en":"380"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The pattern is: subtract 5, then multiply by 2.<br>100 − 5 = 95<br>95 × 2 = 190<br>190 − 5 = 185<br>185 × 2 = 370<br>370 − 5 = 365<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 365.</b>","hi":"पैटर्न है: 5 घटाइए, फिर 2 से गुणा कीजिए।<br>100 − 5 = 95<br>95 × 2 = 190<br>190 − 5 = 185<br>185 × 2 = 370<br>370 − 5 = 365<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 365 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000071585","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Assuming that the data given in the statement are definitely true, which of the following conclusions can be logically deduced from the given statements.<br><b>Statement:</b> Electricity bills will increase by 15% starting next month.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Households should reduce consumption.<br>II. The electricity board is increasing rates. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यह मानते हुए कि कथन में दिया गया विवरण निश्चित रूप से सत्य है, निम्नलिखित में से कौन-से निष्कर्ष दिए गए कथनों से तार्किक रूप से निकाले जा सकते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b> अगले महीने से बिजली के बिल 15% बढ़ेंगे।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. घरों को खपत कम करनी चाहिए।<br>II. बिजली बोर्ड दरें बढ़ा रहा है। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only II follows","hi":"केवल II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both follow","hi":"दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither follows","hi":"कोई नहीं निकलता"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"If the bills are going to rise by 15%, the only way this can happen is that the electricity board is increasing its rates — conclusion II follows directly.<br>Since the bills are becoming costlier, it logically follows that households should cut down their consumption to control the expense — conclusion I also follows.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Both follow.</b>","hi":"यदि बिल 15% बढ़ने वाले हैं, तो यह तभी संभव है जब बिजली बोर्ड अपनी दरें बढ़ा रहा हो — निष्कर्ष II सीधे निकलता है।<br>चूँकि बिल महँगे हो रहे हैं, इसलिए तार्किक रूप से यह भी निकलता है कि घरों को खर्च नियंत्रित करने के लिए अपनी खपत कम करनी चाहिए — निष्कर्ष I भी निकलता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): दोनों निकलते हैं।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000071586","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What should come at the place of question mark? : <b>2, 6, 18, 54, 162, ?</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न के स्थान पर क्या आना चाहिए? : <b>2, 6, 18, 54, 162, ?</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"486"},"2":{"en":"468"},"3":{"en":"482"},"4":{"en":"492"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Every term is 3 times the previous term:<br>2 × 3 = 6<br>6 × 3 = 18<br>18 × 3 = 54<br>54 × 3 = 162<br>162 × 3 = 486<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 486.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद अपने पूर्व पद का 3 गुना है:<br>2 × 3 = 6<br>6 × 3 = 18<br>18 × 3 = 54<br>54 × 3 = 162<br>162 × 3 = 486<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 486 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000071587","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"Some of the equations are provided below with symbols and mathematical relations; you have to check which of the following combination is correct.<br>If A ⤵ B = (A + B + AB) ÷ A, find <b>3 ⤵ 6</b>. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"नीचे कुछ समीकरण प्रतीकों और गणितीय संबंधों के साथ दिए गए हैं; आपको जाँचना है कि निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा संयोजन सही है।<br>यदि A ⤵ B = (A + B + AB) ÷ A है, तो <b>3 ⤵ 6</b> ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7"},"2":{"en":"6"},"3":{"en":"8"},"4":{"en":"9"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"A ⤵ B = (A + B + AB) ÷ A<br>Put A = 3 and B = 6:<br>(3 + 6 + 3 × 6) ÷ 3<br>= (3 + 6 + 18) ÷ 3<br>= 27 ÷ 3 = 9<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 9.</b>","hi":"A ⤵ B = (A + B + AB) ÷ A<br>A = 3 तथा B = 6 रखने पर:<br>(3 + 6 + 3 × 6) ÷ 3<br>= (3 + 6 + 18) ÷ 3<br>= 27 ÷ 3 = 9<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 9 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000071588","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"In the following question, select the word from the given alternatives which cannot be formed using the letters of the given word.<br><b>MOUNTAINOUS</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में दिए गए विकल्पों में से वह शब्द चुनिए जो दिए गए शब्द के अक्षरों से नहीं बनाया जा सकता।<br><b>MOUNTAINOUS</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"STAIN"},"2":{"en":"MOIST"},"3":{"en":"AMOUNT"},"4":{"en":"MASTER"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The letters available in MOUNTAINOUS are M, O, U, N, T, A, I, S (with S twice and O twice).<br>STAIN → S, T, A, I, N ✓<br>MOIST → M, O, I, S, T ✓<br>AMOUNT → A, M, O, U, N, T ✓<br>MASTER needs M, A, S, T, E, R — the letters E and R do not occur in MOUNTAINOUS.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): MASTER.</b>","hi":"MOUNTAINOUS में उपलब्ध अक्षर हैं M, O, U, N, T, A, I, S (S दो बार तथा O दो बार)।<br>STAIN → S, T, A, I, N ✓<br>MOIST → M, O, I, S, T ✓<br>AMOUNT → A, M, O, U, N, T ✓<br>MASTER के लिए M, A, S, T, E, R चाहिए — अक्षर E और R, MOUNTAINOUS में नहीं हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): MASTER है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000071589","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Some social issues, problems and their solutions are provided to you as a statement; you have to mark the logical action that can be taken under these conditions.<br>When you disagree with a decision made by your team, the best approach is to: [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कुछ सामाजिक मुद्दे, समस्याएँ और उनके समाधान कथन के रूप में दिए गए हैं; आपको उस तार्किक कार्रवाई को चिह्नित करना है जो इन परिस्थितियों में की जा सकती है।<br>जब आप अपनी टीम के किसी निर्णय से असहमत हों, तो सर्वोत्तम तरीका है: [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Publicly oppose the decision in the next meeting","hi":"अगली बैठक में निर्णय का सार्वजनिक रूप से विरोध करें"},"2":{"en":"Privately express your concerns to the decision-maker with alternative suggestions","hi":"निर्णय लेने वाले व्यक्ति से निजी तौर पर अपनी चिंताएँ और वैकल्पिक सुझाव बताएँ"},"3":{"en":"Passively resist implementing the decision","hi":"निर्णय को लागू करने का निष्क्रिय विरोध करें"},"4":{"en":"Complain about the decision to other team members","hi":"अन्य टीम सदस्यों से निर्णय की शिकायत करें"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Disagreeing with a team decision should not turn into public confrontation or silent resistance, because both damage the team’s work.<br>Sharing your concerns privately with the decision-maker, along with alternative suggestions, keeps the discussion constructive and gives the decision a fair chance of improvement.<br>The other three options create conflict or obstruct the work of the team.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Privately express your concerns to the decision-maker with alternative suggestions.</b>","hi":"टीम के निर्णय से असहमति को सार्वजनिक टकराव या मौन विरोध में नहीं बदलना चाहिए, क्योंकि दोनों टीम के कार्य को हानि पहुँचाते हैं।<br>निर्णय लेने वाले व्यक्ति से निजी रूप से अपनी चिंताएँ तथा वैकल्पिक सुझाव साझा करना चर्चा को रचनात्मक बनाए रखता है और निर्णय को सुधार का उचित अवसर देता है।<br>शेष तीन विकल्प टकराव पैदा करते हैं या टीम के काम को बाधित करते हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): निर्णय लेने वाले व्यक्ति से निजी तौर पर अपनी चिंताएँ और वैकल्पिक सुझाव बताएँ।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000071590","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Direction: Analyse the statement carefully and determine which of the given conclusions logically follows.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The university established a dedicated startup incubation centre after observing that several student-led projects failed due to lack of mentorship and financial guidance.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Every student project requires financial investment to succeed.<br>II. Lack of mentorship may contribute to project failure. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निर्देश: कथन का ध्यानपूर्वक विश्लेषण कीजिए और निर्धारित कीजिए कि दिए गए निष्कर्षों में से कौन-सा तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>विश्वविद्यालय ने यह देखने के बाद कि कई छात्र-नेतृत्व वाली परियोजनाएँ मार्गदर्शन तथा वित्तीय सलाह की कमी के कारण विफल हुईं, एक समर्पित स्टार्टअप इनक्यूबेशन केंद्र स्थापित किया।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. प्रत्येक छात्र परियोजना को सफल होने के लिए वित्तीय निवेश आवश्यक है।<br>II. मार्गदर्शन की कमी परियोजना की विफलता में योगदान दे सकती है। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only II follows","hi":"केवल II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both follow","hi":"दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither follows","hi":"कोई नहीं निकलता"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The statement itself says that several projects failed due to lack of mentorship and financial guidance, so lack of mentorship can indeed contribute to failure — conclusion II follows.<br>Conclusion I says ‘every’ student project needs financial investment, which is too sweeping and is not stated anywhere.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Only II follows.</b>","hi":"कथन स्वयं कहता है कि कई परियोजनाएँ मार्गदर्शन तथा वित्तीय सलाह की कमी के कारण विफल हुईं, अतः मार्गदर्शन की कमी विफलता में योगदान दे सकती है — निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।<br>निष्कर्ष I कहता है कि ‘प्रत्येक’ छात्र परियोजना को वित्तीय निवेश चाहिए, जो अत्यधिक व्यापक है और कथन में कहीं नहीं कहा गया।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): केवल II निकलता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000071591","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">7</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">72</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">?</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">24</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानिए और तदनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">5</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">7</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">72</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">?</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 8px\">24</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"44"},"2":{"en":"36"},"3":{"en":"28"},"4":{"en":"52"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Column-wise pattern: the third number is the square of the second number minus the square of the first number.<br>Column I: 9<sup>2</sup> − 3<sup>2</sup> = 81 − 9 = 72 ✓<br>Column III: 7<sup>2</sup> − 5<sup>2</sup> = 49 − 25 = 24 ✓<br>Column II: 8<sup>2</sup> − 6<sup>2</sup> = 64 − 36 = 28<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 28.</b>","hi":"स्तंभ-वार पैटर्न: तीसरी संख्या दूसरी संख्या के वर्ग में से पहली संख्या का वर्ग घटाने पर प्राप्त होती है।<br>स्तंभ I: 9<sup>2</sup> − 3<sup>2</sup> = 81 − 9 = 72 ✓<br>स्तंभ III: 7<sup>2</sup> − 5<sup>2</sup> = 49 − 25 = 24 ✓<br>स्तंभ II: 8<sup>2</sup> − 6<sup>2</sup> = 64 − 36 = 28<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 28 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000071592","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option which is exactly similar to:<br><b>M/s Cliffton &amp; Sons, 22nd Nov' 1999, Sector-17, Chandigarh-160017</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो निम्नलिखित के ठीक समान है:<br><b>M/s Cliffton &amp; Sons, 22nd Nov' 1999, Sector-17, Chandigarh-160017</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"M/s Cliffton & Sons, 22nd Nov' 1999, Sector-17, Chandigarh-160018"},"2":{"en":"M/s Cliffton & Sons, 22nd Nov' 1999, Sector-17, Chandigarh-160017"},"3":{"en":"M/s Cliffton & Sons, 22nd Nov' 1999, Sector 17, Chandigarh-160017"},"4":{"en":"M/s Cliffton and Sons, 22nd Nov' 1999, Sector-17, Chandigarh-160017"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Compare each option with the given address word by word:<br>Option (1): the PIN code is 160018 instead of 160017.<br>Option (3): the hyphen in ‘Sector-17’ is missing.<br>Option (4): ‘&amp;’ has been written as ‘and’.<br>Only option (2) matches the given address in every respect — same name, same date, same sector with the hyphen and the same PIN code.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): M/s Cliffton &amp; Sons, 22nd Nov' 1999, Sector-17, Chandigarh-160017.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक विकल्प की दिए गए पते से शब्द-दर-शब्द तुलना कीजिए:<br>विकल्प (1): पिन कोड 160017 के स्थान पर 160018 है।<br>विकल्प (3): ‘Sector-17’ में हाइफ़न नहीं है।<br>विकल्प (4): ‘&amp;’ के स्थान पर ‘and’ लिखा है।<br>केवल विकल्प (2) हर दृष्टि से दिए गए पते से मेल खाता है — वही नाम, वही तिथि, हाइफ़न सहित वही सेक्टर तथा वही पिन कोड।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): M/s Cliffton &amp; Sons, 22nd Nov' 1999, Sector-17, Chandigarh-160017 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000071593","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"Given that X ∈ {2, 4, 6} and Y ∈ {1, 3, 5}, find the maximum possible value of the following mathematical operational expression.<br><b>(X<sup>2</sup> − Y) / Y</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यह दिया गया है कि X ∈ {2, 4, 6} तथा Y ∈ {1, 3, 5} है; निम्नलिखित गणितीय संक्रिया व्यंजक का अधिकतम संभावित मान ज्ञात कीजिए।<br><b>(X<sup>2</sup> − Y) / Y</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"35"},"2":{"en":"23"},"3":{"en":"11"},"4":{"en":"17"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The value (X<sup>2</sup> − Y)/Y becomes largest when X is as large as possible and Y is as small as possible.<br>Take X = 6 and Y = 1:<br>(6<sup>2</sup> − 1)/1 = (36 − 1)/1 = 35<br>Check the next best case, X = 6, Y = 3 → (36 − 3)/3 = 11, which is much smaller.<br>Hence the maximum value is 35.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 35.</b>","hi":"(X<sup>2</sup> − Y)/Y का मान तब सबसे अधिक होता है जब X यथासंभव बड़ा और Y यथासंभव छोटा हो।<br>X = 6 तथा Y = 1 लेने पर:<br>(6<sup>2</sup> − 1)/1 = (36 − 1)/1 = 35<br>अगली संभावना, X = 6, Y = 3 → (36 − 3)/3 = 11, जो बहुत कम है।<br>अतः अधिकतम मान 35 है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 35 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000071594","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"In the following question a statement is given followed by some assumptions. Read the assumptions carefully and choose the appropriate option.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Please read the instructions carefully before attempting the examination.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. A student may make mistakes if the instructions are not read carefully.<br>II. It is important to perform correctly in the examination. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन दिया गया है, जिसके बाद कुछ पूर्वधारणाएँ हैं। पूर्वधारणाओं को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उपयुक्त विकल्प चुनिए।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>परीक्षा का प्रयास करने से पहले कृपया निर्देशों को ध्यान से पढ़ें।<br><b>पूर्वधारणाएँ:</b><br>I. यदि निर्देश ध्यान से न पढ़े जाएँ तो विद्यार्थी गलतियाँ कर सकता है।<br>II. परीक्षा में सही प्रदर्शन करना महत्वपूर्ण है। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I is implicit.","hi":"केवल I निहित है।"},"2":{"en":"Only II is implicit.","hi":"केवल II निहित है।"},"3":{"en":"Neither I nor II is implicit.","hi":"न तो I और न ही II निहित है।"},"4":{"en":"Both I and II are implicit.","hi":"I और II दोनों निहित हैं।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The instruction to read the notice carefully is given only because, without careful reading, mistakes are likely — Assumption I is implicit.<br>The very purpose of giving such an instruction is that correct performance in the examination matters — Assumption II is also implicit.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Both I and II are implicit.</b>","hi":"निर्देशों को ध्यान से पढ़ने का आदेश इसीलिए दिया गया है कि सावधानी से न पढ़ने पर गलतियाँ हो सकती हैं — पूर्वधारणा I निहित है।<br>ऐसा निर्देश देने का उद्देश्य ही यह है कि परीक्षा में सही प्रदर्शन महत्वपूर्ण है — पूर्वधारणा II भी निहित है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): I और II दोनों निहित हैं।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000071595","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The state government has announced subsidies for rooftop solar panels to encourage the adoption of renewable energy sources.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. The government wants more people to use renewable energy.<br>II. Conventional energy sources will immediately become obsolete.<br>III. Financial incentives may encourage the adoption of solar energy. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन दिया गया है, जिसके बाद कुछ अनुमान हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, चाहे वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों के विपरीत प्रतीत हो। अनुमानों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-से कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>राज्य सरकार ने नवीकरणीय ऊर्जा स्रोतों को अपनाने को प्रोत्साहित करने के लिए छत पर लगने वाले सोलर पैनलों हेतु सब्सिडी की घोषणा की है।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. सरकार चाहती है कि अधिक से अधिक लोग नवीकरणीय ऊर्जा का उपयोग करें।<br>II. पारंपरिक ऊर्जा स्रोत तुरंत अप्रचलित हो जाएँगे।<br>III. वित्तीय प्रोत्साहन सोलर ऊर्जा को अपनाने में सहायक हो सकते हैं। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only inferences I and II follow.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I और II निकलते हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Only inferences II and III follow.","hi":"केवल अनुमान II और III निकलते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"All inferences follow.","hi":"सभी अनुमान निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Only inferences I and III follow.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I और III निकलते हैं।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The statement says that subsidies are being given ‘to encourage the adoption of renewable energy’, so the government clearly wants more people to use renewable energy — inference I follows.<br>It also shows that financial incentives are being used for this purpose, i.e. such incentives may encourage the use of solar energy — inference III follows.<br>Nothing is said about conventional sources becoming obsolete, and certainly not ‘immediately’ — inference II does not follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Only inferences I and III follow.</b>","hi":"कथन कहता है कि सब्सिडी ‘नवीकरणीय ऊर्जा को अपनाने को प्रोत्साहित करने’ के लिए दी जा रही है, अतः सरकार स्पष्ट रूप से चाहती है कि अधिक लोग नवीकरणीय ऊर्जा का उपयोग करें — अनुमान I निकलता है।<br>इससे यह भी पता चलता है कि इस उद्देश्य के लिए वित्तीय प्रोत्साहन दिया जा रहा है, अर्थात् ऐसे प्रोत्साहन सोलर ऊर्जा के उपयोग को बढ़ावा दे सकते हैं — अनुमान III निकलता है।<br>पारंपरिक स्रोतों के अप्रचलित होने के बारे में कुछ नहीं कहा गया, और ‘तुरंत’ तो बिल्कुल नहीं — अनुमान II नहीं निकलता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): केवल अनुमान I और III निकलते हैं।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000071596","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Extensive use of pesticides in agricultural production contaminates soil and water, persists in crops, and ultimately enters the food chain, thereby posing a threat to human beings.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. Excessive use of pesticides in agricultural production is harmful to human health.<br>II. Excessive use of pesticides in agricultural production can adversely affect water quality.<br>III. Pesticide contamination can enter the human body through the food chain. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन दिया गया है, जिसके बाद कुछ अनुमान हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, चाहे वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों के विपरीत प्रतीत हो। अनुमानों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-से कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कृषि उत्पादन में कीटनाशकों का अत्यधिक उपयोग मिट्टी और जल को दूषित करता है, फसलों में बना रहता है और अंततः खाद्य श्रृंखला में प्रवेश कर जाता है, जिससे मनुष्यों के लिए खतरा उत्पन्न होता है।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. कृषि उत्पादन में कीटनाशकों का अत्यधिक उपयोग मानव स्वास्थ्य के लिए हानिकारक है।<br>II. कृषि उत्पादन में कीटनाशकों का अत्यधिक उपयोग जल की गुणवत्ता पर प्रतिकूल प्रभाव डाल सकता है।<br>III. कीटनाशक संदूषण खाद्य श्रृंखला के माध्यम से मानव शरीर में प्रवेश कर सकता है। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only inferences I and II follow.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I और II निकलते हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Only inferences I and III follow.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I और III निकलते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Only inferences II and III follow.","hi":"केवल अनुमान II और III निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"All inferences follow.","hi":"सभी अनुमान निकलते हैं।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The statement says that pesticides ultimately pose a threat to human beings, so excessive use of pesticides is harmful to human health — inference I follows.<br>It says that pesticides contaminate water, so water quality is adversely affected — inference II follows.<br>It also says that pesticides enter the food chain, which is how they reach the human body — inference III follows.<br>Hence all the three inferences follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): All inferences follow.</b>","hi":"कथन कहता है कि कीटनाशक अंततः मनुष्यों के लिए खतरा उत्पन्न करते हैं, अतः कीटनाशकों का अत्यधिक उपयोग मानव स्वास्थ्य के लिए हानिकारक है — अनुमान I निकलता है।<br>कथन कहता है कि कीटनाशक जल को दूषित करते हैं, अतः जल की गुणवत्ता पर प्रतिकूल प्रभाव पड़ता है — अनुमान II निकलता है।<br>यह भी कहा गया है कि कीटनाशक खाद्य श्रृंखला में प्रवेश करते हैं, जिससे वे मानव शरीर तक पहुँचते हैं — अनुमान III निकलता है।<br>अतः तीनों अनुमान निकलते हैं।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): सभी अनुमान निकलते हैं।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000071597","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"A corporate executive must announce an impending company-wide budget cut that will significantly affect several departments. Employees are visibly anxious, highly disruptive rumours are spreading rapidly across the office, and general workplace uncertainty is increasing by the day.<br>What communication strategy by the executive demonstrates the highest level of emotional intelligence (EQ) to maintain corporate trust and minimize operational disruption? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक कॉर्पोरेट अधिकारी को कंपनी-व्यापी आगामी बजट कटौती की घोषणा करनी है जो कई विभागों को महत्वपूर्ण रूप से प्रभावित करेगी। कर्मचारी स्पष्ट रूप से चिंतित हैं, कार्यालय में अत्यधिक भ्रामक अफवाहें तेज़ी से फैल रही हैं और कार्यस्थल की अनिश्चितता दिन-प्रतिदिन बढ़ रही है।<br>कॉर्पोरेट विश्वास बनाए रखने तथा परिचालन व्यवधान को न्यूनतम करने के लिए अधिकारी की कौन-सी संचार रणनीति भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता (EQ) का उच्चतम स्तर दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Postpone all official communication indefinitely until every financial detail is finalized, keeping executive board discussions entirely hidden.","hi":"जब तक हर वित्तीय विवरण अंतिम रूप न ले लिया जाए, सभी आधिकारिक संचार को अनिश्चित काल के लिए टाल दें और कार्यकारी बोर्ड की चर्चाओं को पूरी तरह गुप्त रखें।"},"2":{"en":"Issue a highly optimistic announcement that highlights only positive growth data while purposefully omitting the budget cuts.","hi":"एक अत्यधिक आशावादी घोषणा जारी करें जिसमें केवल सकारात्मक विकास के आँकड़े बताए जाएँ और बजट कटौती को जानबूझकर छोड़ दिया जाए।"},"3":{"en":"Delegate the announcement to department managers, letting them address their employees' panic independently without central guidance.","hi":"घोषणा विभागीय प्रबंधकों को सौंप दें और उन्हें बिना केंद्रीय मार्गदर्शन के अपने कर्मचारियों की घबराहट स्वयं संभालने दें।"},"4":{"en":"Deliver a direct, centralized message that communicates known facts transparently, validates employee anxiety, and outlines strategic logic.","hi":"एक स्पष्ट, केंद्रीकृत संदेश दें जिसमें ज्ञात तथ्य पारदर्शी रूप से बताए जाएँ, कर्मचारियों की चिंता को मान्यता दी जाए और रणनीतिक तर्क स्पष्ट किया जाए।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Emotional intelligence means recognising the feelings of others and dealing with them honestly and promptly.<br>Keeping silent or hiding the cuts increases rumours and anxiety, while delegating the message without guidance spreads confusion.<br>A direct, transparent, company-wide message that accepts the anxiety of the employees and explains the logic behind the decision builds trust and limits disruption.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Deliver a direct, centralized message that communicates known facts transparently, validates employee anxiety, and outlines strategic logic.</b>","hi":"भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता का अर्थ है दूसरों की भावनाओं को पहचानना तथा उनसे ईमानदारी और तत्परता से निपटना।<br>चुप रहने या कटौती छिपाने से अफवाहें और चिंता बढ़ती है, तथा बिना मार्गदर्शन के संदेश सौंपने से भ्रम फैलता है।<br>सीधा, पारदर्शी और कंपनी-व्यापी संदेश, जो कर्मचारियों की चिंता को स्वीकार करता है और निर्णय के पीछे का तर्क समझाता है, विश्वास बनाता है और व्यवधान सीमित करता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): एक स्पष्ट, केंद्रीकृत संदेश दें जिसमें ज्ञात तथ्य पारदर्शी रूप से बताए जाएँ, कर्मचारियों की चिंता को मान्यता दी जाए और रणनीतिक तर्क स्पष्ट किया जाए।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000071598","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"Read the given conditions carefully and determine the appropriate outcome for the case provided. If any exception applies, identify the authority to whom the case should be referred.<br><b>Criteria for Government Tender Eligibility:</b><br>(i) Must have state registration.<br>(ii) Annual turnover must be above ₹2 Crore.<br><b>Exceptions:</b><br><b>Exception (A):</b> If the turnover is below ₹2 Crore but the company has received a national quality award, refer the case to the Tender Committee.<br><b>Exception (B):</b> If the company meets criteria (i) and (ii) but is currently under blacklisting proceedings by another state department, refer the case to the Legal Compliance Bureau.<br><b>Case:</b> The company turnover is ₹1.8 Crore, the company holds a national quality award, and possesses state registration. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दी गई शर्तों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और दिए गए मामले के लिए उपयुक्त परिणाम निर्धारित कीजिए। यदि कोई अपवाद लागू होता है, तो उस प्राधिकरण की पहचान कीजिए जिसे मामला भेजा जाना चाहिए।<br><b>सरकारी निविदा पात्रता के मानदंड:</b><br>(i) राज्य में पंजीकरण होना चाहिए।<br>(ii) वार्षिक कारोबार ₹2 करोड़ से अधिक होना चाहिए।<br><b>अपवाद:</b><br><b>अपवाद (A):</b> यदि कारोबार ₹2 करोड़ से कम है किंतु कंपनी को राष्ट्रीय गुणवत्ता पुरस्कार प्राप्त है, तो मामला निविदा समिति को भेजें।<br><b>अपवाद (B):</b> यदि कंपनी मानदंड (i) और (ii) पूरा करती है किंतु किसी अन्य राज्य विभाग द्वारा ब्लैकलिस्टिंग की कार्यवाही चल रही है, तो मामला विधिक अनुपालन ब्यूरो को भेजें।<br><b>मामला:</b> कंपनी का कारोबार ₹1.8 करोड़ है, कंपनी के पास राष्ट्रीय गुणवत्ता पुरस्कार है तथा राज्य में पंजीकरण भी है। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tender eligibility to be approved","hi":"निविदा पात्रता स्वीकृत की जाए"},"2":{"en":"Case to be referred to the Tender Committee","hi":"मामला निविदा समिति को भेजा जाए"},"3":{"en":"Tender application to be rejected","hi":"निविदा आवेदन अस्वीकार किया जाए"},"4":{"en":"Case to be referred to the Legal Compliance Bureau","hi":"मामला विधिक अनुपालन ब्यूरो को भेजा जाए"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Condition (i): state registration — satisfied.<br>Condition (ii): turnover above ₹2 Crore — the turnover is ₹1.8 Crore, so this condition is not satisfied.<br>Exception (B) does not apply because the company does not meet condition (ii).<br>Exception (A) applies exactly: turnover below ₹2 Crore, but the company holds a national quality award — so the case must be referred to the Tender Committee.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Case to be referred to the Tender Committee.</b>","hi":"शर्त (i): राज्य में पंजीकरण — पूरी होती है।<br>शर्त (ii): कारोबार ₹2 करोड़ से अधिक — कारोबार ₹1.8 करोड़ है, अतः यह शर्त पूरी नहीं होती।<br>अपवाद (B) लागू नहीं होता, क्योंकि कंपनी शर्त (ii) पूरी नहीं करती।<br>अपवाद (A) ठीक लागू होता है: कारोबार ₹2 करोड़ से कम है, किंतु कंपनी के पास राष्ट्रीय गुणवत्ता पुरस्कार है — अतः मामला निविदा समिति को भेजा जाना चाहिए।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): मामला निविदा समिति को भेजा जाए।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000071599","section":"REASONING","topic":"Matrix","question":{"en":"Which of the following rows/columns are connected/related with each other in some way?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rows</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\" colspan=\"5\">Columns</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">729</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">64</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">81</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">343</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">49</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">216</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">125</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">64</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी पंक्तियाँ/स्तंभ किसी प्रकार से एक-दूसरे से जुड़े/संबंधित हैं?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">पंक्तियाँ</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\" colspan=\"5\">स्तंभ</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"></td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">729</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">64</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">81</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">343</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">49</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">216</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">125</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">25</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">64</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Columns I, II and V","hi":"स्तंभ I, II और V"},"2":{"en":"Columns II, IV and V","hi":"स्तंभ II, IV और V"},"3":{"en":"Columns I, II and IV","hi":"स्तंभ I, II और IV"},"4":{"en":"Columns II, III and IV","hi":"स्तंभ II, III और IV"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Column I = 9, 7, 6, 5, 4<br>Column V = 81, 49, 36, 25, 16 = 9<sup>2</sup>, 7<sup>2</sup>, 6<sup>2</sup>, 5<sup>2</sup>, 4<sup>2</sup> — the squares of column I.<br>Column II = 729, 343, 216, 125, 64 = 9<sup>3</sup>, 7<sup>3</sup>, 6<sup>3</sup>, 5<sup>3</sup>, 4<sup>3</sup> — the cubes of column I.<br>So columns I, II and V are related to one another (the same base numbers raised to the powers 1, 3 and 2).<br>Columns III and IV do not follow this pattern.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Columns I, II and V.</b>","hi":"स्तंभ I = 9, 7, 6, 5, 4<br>स्तंभ V = 81, 49, 36, 25, 16 = 9<sup>2</sup>, 7<sup>2</sup>, 6<sup>2</sup>, 5<sup>2</sup>, 4<sup>2</sup> — अर्थात् स्तंभ I के वर्ग।<br>स्तंभ II = 729, 343, 216, 125, 64 = 9<sup>3</sup>, 7<sup>3</sup>, 6<sup>3</sup>, 5<sup>3</sup>, 4<sup>3</sup> — अर्थात् स्तंभ I के घन।<br>अतः स्तंभ I, II और V एक-दूसरे से संबंधित हैं (समान आधार संख्याओं की घातें 1, 3 तथा 2)।<br>स्तंभ III और IV इस पैटर्न का पालन नहीं करते।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): स्तंभ I, II और V है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000071600","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"Read the criteria given for a position along with some exceptions and then decide what decision should be taken for the case given.<br><b>The following are the requirements for recruiting Tech Corp:</b><br>A. At least 75% in class 10th and 12th.<br>B. At least 70% in Mechanical or Civil Engineering.<br>C. Age not more than 25 years as on October 09, 2017.<br>D. At least 60% in selection test.<br>E. CAD course from a reputed institute.<br><b>Exception 1:</b> Fails C only + more than 1 year experience → Refer to Managing Director.<br><b>Exception 2:</b> Fails E only + ready to pay ₹35,000+ + at least 75% in graduation → Refer to Chairman.<br><b>Case:</b> Nitin has scored 63% marks in the selection test and graduated with 74% marks in Mechanical Engineering. He has completed a CAD course at NIT and was born on 17/10/1994. He got 350 marks out of 500 in class 10th and 900 marks out of 1200 in class 12th. What will be decided in his case? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी पद के लिए दिए गए मानदंडों तथा कुछ अपवादों को पढ़िए और फिर दिए गए मामले में क्या निर्णय लिया जाना चाहिए, यह तय कीजिए।<br><b>टेक कॉर्प में भर्ती के लिए निम्नलिखित आवश्यकताएँ हैं:</b><br>A. कक्षा 10वीं और 12वीं में कम से कम 75%।<br>B. मैकेनिकल या सिविल इंजीनियरिंग में कम से कम 70%।<br>C. 09 अक्टूबर, 2017 को आयु 25 वर्ष से अधिक न हो।<br>D. चयन परीक्षा में कम से कम 60%।<br>E. किसी प्रतिष्ठित संस्थान से CAD कोर्स।<br><b>अपवाद 1:</b> केवल C में असफल + 1 वर्ष से अधिक अनुभव → प्रबंध निदेशक को भेजें।<br><b>अपवाद 2:</b> केवल E में असफल + ₹35,000+ देने को तैयार + स्नातक में कम से कम 75% → अध्यक्ष को भेजें।<br><b>मामला:</b> नितिन ने चयन परीक्षा में 63% अंक प्राप्त किए तथा मैकेनिकल इंजीनियरिंग में 74% अंकों के साथ स्नातक किया। उन्होंने NIT से CAD कोर्स पूरा किया है और उनका जन्म 17/10/1994 को हुआ था। उन्होंने कक्षा 10वीं में 500 में से 350 अंक तथा कक्षा 12वीं में 1200 में से 900 अंक प्राप्त किए। उनके मामले में क्या निर्णय लिया जाएगा? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Refer to the Managing Director.","hi":"प्रबंध निदेशक को भेजें।"},"2":{"en":"Refer to the Chairman.","hi":"अध्यक्ष को भेजें।"},"3":{"en":"Candidate is selected.","hi":"अभ्यर्थी चयनित है।"},"4":{"en":"Candidate is not selected.","hi":"अभ्यर्थी चयनित नहीं है।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Check every criterion:<br>A. 10th → 350/500 = 70% (needs 75%) ✗ ; 12th → 900/1200 = 75% ✓<br>B. 74% in Mechanical Engineering ✓<br>C. Born 17/10/1994, so on 09/10/2017 he is 22 years 11 months — not more than 25 ✓<br>D. 63% in the selection test ✓<br>E. CAD course from NIT ✓<br>He fails criterion A only (10th marks). Exception 1 applies only when the candidate fails C only, and Exception 2 only when he fails E only, so neither exception applies and the candidate cannot be selected.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Candidate is not selected.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक मानदंड की जाँच कीजिए:<br>A. 10वीं → 350/500 = 70% (75% चाहिए) ✗ ; 12वीं → 900/1200 = 75% ✓<br>B. मैकेनिकल इंजीनियरिंग में 74% ✓<br>C. जन्म 17/10/1994, अतः 09/10/2017 को आयु 22 वर्ष 11 माह है — 25 से अधिक नहीं ✓<br>D. चयन परीक्षा में 63% ✓<br>E. NIT से CAD कोर्स ✓<br>वे केवल मानदंड A (10वीं के अंक) में असफल हैं। अपवाद 1 तभी लागू होता है जब केवल C में असफलता हो और अपवाद 2 तभी जब केवल E में असफलता हो, अतः कोई अपवाद लागू नहीं होता और अभ्यर्थी चयनित नहीं हो सकता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): अभ्यर्थी चयनित नहीं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000071601","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"In the following question two statements are given and these statements are followed by two conclusions. You have to take the given two statements to be true even if they seem to be at variance from commonly known facts. Read the conclusions and then decide which of the given conclusions logically follows from the two given statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>Some roses are flowers.<br>Some flowers are plants.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. All plants are flowers.<br>II. Some plants are flowers. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में दो कथन दिए गए हैं और इन कथनों के बाद दो निष्कर्ष हैं। दिए गए दोनों कथनों को सत्य मानना है, चाहे वे सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न प्रतीत हों। निष्कर्षों को पढ़िए और फिर निर्णय कीजिए कि दिए गए निष्कर्षों में से कौन-सा दोनों कथनों से तार्किक रूप से निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कुछ गुलाब, फूल हैं।<br>कुछ फूल, पौधे हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सभी पौधे, फूल हैं।<br>II. कुछ पौधे, फूल हैं। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"‘Some flowers are plants’ means that the flowers which are plants are also plants which are flowers; the two classes overlap.<br>So ‘Some plants are flowers’ is only the conversion of the given statement and it definitely follows — conclusion II follows.<br>‘Some flowers are plants’ cannot be stretched to ‘All plants are flowers’, so conclusion I does not follow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Only conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"‘कुछ फूल, पौधे हैं’ का अर्थ है कि जो फूल पौधे हैं, वे पौधे फूल भी हैं; दोनों वर्ग अतिव्यापी हैं।<br>अतः ‘कुछ पौधे, फूल हैं’ दिए गए कथन का केवल परिवर्तन (conversion) है और निश्चित रूप से निकलता है — निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।<br>‘कुछ फूल, पौधे हैं’ से ‘सभी पौधे, फूल हैं’ नहीं निकलता, इसलिए निष्कर्ष I नहीं निकलता।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000071602","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>The university has introduced a mandatory 'Communication Skills' course for all final-year engineering students to increase their employability in the corporate sector.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. Proficiency in communication skills is a significant factor in determining the success of a candidate during corporate recruitment.<br>II. Students currently lack the necessary communication proficiency required by the corporate sector. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए कथन तथा उस पर आधारित निम्नलिखित पूर्वधारणाओं को ध्यान से पढ़िए। निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सी पूर्वधारणाएँ कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>विश्वविद्यालय ने कॉर्पोरेट क्षेत्र में रोजगार-क्षमता बढ़ाने के लिए सभी अंतिम वर्ष के इंजीनियरिंग छात्रों के लिए ‘संचार कौशल’ का अनिवार्य कोर्स शुरू किया है।<br><b>पूर्वधारणाएँ:</b><br>I. कॉर्पोरेट भर्ती के दौरान उम्मीदवार की सफलता निर्धारित करने में संचार कौशल में दक्षता एक महत्वपूर्ण कारक है।<br>II. छात्रों में वर्तमान में कॉर्पोरेट क्षेत्र द्वारा अपेक्षित संचार दक्षता का अभाव है। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल पूर्वधारणा I निहित है"},"2":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"पूर्वधारणा I और II दोनों निहित हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल पूर्वधारणा II निहित है"},"4":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो पूर्वधारणा I और न ही II निहित है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The course is introduced ‘to increase employability in the corporate sector’, which means the university believes that communication skills matter in corporate recruitment — Assumption I is implicit.<br>But nothing in the statement says that the students are presently deficient in communication skills; the course may simply be meant to improve an already existing ability — Assumption II is not implicit.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only Assumption I is implicit.</b>","hi":"यह कोर्स ‘कॉर्पोरेट क्षेत्र में रोजगार-क्षमता बढ़ाने के लिए’ शुरू किया गया है, अर्थात् विश्वविद्यालय मानता है कि कॉर्पोरेट भर्ती में संचार कौशल महत्वपूर्ण है — पूर्वधारणा I निहित है।<br>किंतु कथन में कहीं नहीं कहा गया कि छात्रों में वर्तमान में संचार कौशल का अभाव है; कोर्स तो पहले से विद्यमान क्षमता को और सुधारने के लिए भी हो सकता है — पूर्वधारणा II निहित नहीं है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल पूर्वधारणा I निहित है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000071603","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"Under a tax scheme, a full rebate applies if taxable income ≤ ₹5,00,000 and returns are filed before the due date; income between ₹5,00,000–₹7,00,000 filed on time gets a 50% rebate. Filing late forfeits the rebate regardless of income.<br><b>Case:</b> taxable income ₹4,80,000, return filed 2 days after the due date. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक कर योजना के अंतर्गत, यदि कर योग्य आय ≤ ₹5,00,000 हो और रिटर्न नियत तिथि से पहले जमा किया गया हो तो पूरी छूट मिलती है; ₹5,00,000–₹7,00,000 के बीच की आय पर समय पर रिटर्न जमा करने पर 50% छूट मिलती है। देर से रिटर्न जमा करने पर आय कुछ भी हो, छूट समाप्त हो जाती है।<br><b>मामला:</b> कर योग्य आय ₹4,80,000, रिटर्न नियत तिथि के 2 दिन बाद जमा किया गया। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Full rebate","hi":"पूरी छूट"},"2":{"en":"25% rebate","hi":"25% छूट"},"3":{"en":"50% rebate","hi":"50% छूट"},"4":{"en":"No rebate","hi":"कोई छूट नहीं"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The taxable income is ₹4,80,000, which is within ₹5,00,000, so the full rebate would normally apply.<br>But the return has been filed 2 days after the due date, and the scheme clearly says that filing late forfeits the rebate regardless of income.<br>Therefore no rebate is admissible.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): No rebate.</b>","hi":"कर योग्य आय ₹4,80,000 है, जो ₹5,00,000 के भीतर है, अतः सामान्यतः पूरी छूट लागू होती।<br>किंतु रिटर्न नियत तिथि के 2 दिन बाद जमा किया गया है और योजना स्पष्ट कहती है कि देर से जमा करने पर आय कुछ भी हो, छूट समाप्त हो जाती है।<br>इसलिए कोई छूट नहीं मिलेगी।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): कोई छूट नहीं।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000071604","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Which of the following letter-clusters will replace the question mark (?) in the given series to make it logically complete?<br><b>AC, EG, IK, MO, QS, UW, ?</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा अक्षर-समूह दी गई श्रृंखला में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर आएगा, जिससे श्रृंखला तार्किक रूप से पूर्ण हो जाए?<br><b>AC, EG, IK, MO, QS, UW, ?</b> [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"YA"},"2":{"en":"YZ"},"3":{"en":"ZB"},"4":{"en":"XZ"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Positions of the letters:<br>AC → 1, 3<br>EG → 5, 7<br>IK → 9, 11<br>MO → 13, 15<br>QS → 17, 19<br>UW → 21, 23<br>Every cluster starts 4 places after the previous cluster’s first letter, and the second letter is 2 more than the first.<br>Next first letter = 21 + 4 = 25 → Y, and the second letter = Y + 2, which after Z comes back to A → YA.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): YA.</b>","hi":"अक्षरों के स्थान:<br>AC → 1, 3<br>EG → 5, 7<br>IK → 9, 11<br>MO → 13, 15<br>QS → 17, 19<br>UW → 21, 23<br>प्रत्येक समूह का पहला अक्षर पिछले समूह के पहले अक्षर से 4 स्थान आगे है और दूसरा अक्षर पहले से 2 अधिक है।<br>अगला पहला अक्षर = 21 + 4 = 25 → Y, और दूसरा अक्षर = Y + 2, जो Z के बाद वर्णमाला में A आता है → YA।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): YA है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000071605","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In each of the following questions, four options have been given, of which three are alike in some way and one is different. Choose the odd one out. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रत्येक प्रश्न में चार विकल्प दिए गए हैं, जिनमें से तीन किसी प्रकार समान हैं और एक भिन्न है। विषम विकल्प चुनिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Turkey – Ankara – Lira","hi":"तुर्की – अंकारा – लीरा"},"2":{"en":"Iran – Tehran – Rial","hi":"ईरान – तेहरान – रियाल"},"3":{"en":"Iraq – Baghdad – Dinar","hi":"इराक – बगदाद – दीनार"},"4":{"en":"Saudi Arabia – Riyadh – Dirham","hi":"सऊदी अरब – रियाद – दिरहम"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Every option gives a country, its capital and its currency.<br>Turkey – Ankara – Lira ✓, Iran – Tehran – Rial ✓, Iraq – Baghdad – Dinar ✓ — in all these the third term is the correct currency.<br>The currency of Saudi Arabia is the Riyal (Saudi Riyal), not the Dirham; the Dirham belongs to the UAE and Morocco.<br>So option (4) is different from the rest.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Saudi Arabia – Riyadh – Dirham.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक विकल्प में देश, उसकी राजधानी और उसकी मुद्रा दी गई है।<br>तुर्की – अंकारा – लीरा ✓, ईरान – तेहरान – रियाल ✓, इराक – बगदाद – दीनार ✓ — इन सभी में तीसरा पद सही मुद्रा है।<br>सऊदी अरब की मुद्रा रियाल (सऊदी रियाल) है, दिरहम नहीं; दिरहम संयुक्त अरब अमीरात और मोरक्को की मुद्रा है।<br>इसलिए विकल्प (4) बाकियों से भिन्न है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): सऊदी अरब – रियाद – दिरहम है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000071606","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Himalayas","question":{"en":"Between which two major mountain ranges is the Valley of Kashmir situated? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कश्मीर घाटी किन दो प्रमुख पर्वत श्रृंखलाओं के बीच स्थित है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ladakh and Zanskar","hi":"लद्दाख तथा ज़ांस्कर"},"2":{"en":"Great Himalayas and Pir Panjal","hi":"वृहद हिमालय तथा पीर पंजाल"},"3":{"en":"Great Himalayas and Zanskar","hi":"वृहद हिमालय तथा ज़ांस्कर"},"4":{"en":"Karakoram and Ladakh","hi":"काराकोरम तथा लद्दाख"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Great Himalayas and Pir Panjal</b><br>The <b>Valley of Kashmir</b> is a structural trough lying between the <b>Great Himalayas</b> in the north-east and the <b>Pir Panjal range</b> in the south-west.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The valley is drained by the <b>Jhelum</b> river and is about <b>135 km long and 32 km wide</b>.<br>• The <b>Pir Panjal</b> range separates the Kashmir valley from the <b>Punjab plains</b> and is crossed by passes such as <b>Banihal and Pir Panjal</b>.<br>• The <b>Great Himalayas</b> include the <b>Nanga Parbat</b> massif, and the <b>Zanskar and Ladakh</b> ranges lie further north-east.<br>• Kashmir is famous for <b>Karewas</b>, lacustrine deposits used for growing saffron and orchards, and for <b>Dal and Wular</b> lakes.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – वृहद हिमालय तथा पीर पंजाल</b><br><b>कश्मीर घाटी</b> एक संरचनात्मक गर्त है जो उत्तर-पूर्व में <b>वृहद हिमालय</b> तथा दक्षिण-पश्चिम में <b>पीर पंजाल श्रेणी</b> के बीच स्थित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह घाटी <b>झेलम</b> नदी से अपवाहित होती है और लगभग <b>135 किमी लंबी तथा 32 किमी चौड़ी</b> है।<br>• <b>पीर पंजाल</b> श्रेणी कश्मीर घाटी को <b>पंजाब के मैदानों</b> से अलग करती है और इसमें <b>बनिहाल तथा पीर पंजाल</b> जैसे दर्रे हैं।<br>• <b>वृहद हिमालय</b> में <b>नंगा परबत</b> समूह आता है, जबकि <b>ज़ांस्कर तथा लद्दाख</b> श्रेणियाँ और उत्तर-पूर्व में हैं।<br>• कश्मीर <b>करीवा</b> नामक सरोवरीय निक्षेपों के लिए प्रसिद्ध है, जहाँ केसर तथा बाग लगाए जाते हैं, और <b>डल एवं वुलर</b> झीलों के लिए भी जाना जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000071607","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Parliament","question":{"en":"Under Article 113 of the Indian Constitution, which House of Parliament has the exclusive power to assent to or refuse any demand for a grant of expenditure? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के अनुच्छेद 113 के अंतर्गत व्यय की मांग पर सहमति देने अथवा अस्वीकार करने की अनन्य शक्ति संसद के किस सदन के पास है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The Rajya Sabha","hi":"राज्यसभा"},"2":{"en":"The Lok Sabha","hi":"लोकसभा"},"3":{"en":"The Joint Parliamentary Committee","hi":"संयुक्त संसदीय समिति"},"4":{"en":"The Cabinet Committee on Political Affairs","hi":"राजनीतिक मामलों की मंत्रिमंडलीय समिति"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – The Lok Sabha</b><br><b>Article 113</b> provides that no demand for a grant shall be made except on the recommendation of the <b>President</b>, and such demands are presented to and voted upon only in the <b>Lok Sabha</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Lok Sabha</b> has exclusive control over <b>Money Bills (Article 110)</b> and over <b>grants and appropriations</b>, while the Rajya Sabha can only recommend changes.<br>• A <b>Money Bill</b> can be introduced only in the Lok Sabha with the President's recommendation, and the Rajya Sabha must return it within <b>14 days</b>.<br>• After the demands are voted, the <b>Appropriation Bill</b> is introduced under Article <b>114</b> to authorise withdrawal from the <b>Consolidated Fund of India</b>.<br>• <b>Cut motions</b> such as policy cut, economy cut and token cut can be moved against a demand for grant in the Lok Sabha.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – लोकसभा</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 113</b> प्रावधान करता है कि <b>राष्ट्रपति</b> की सिफारिश के बिना कोई अनुदान मांग नहीं की जाएगी, तथा ऐसी मांगें केवल <b>लोकसभा</b> में प्रस्तुत की जाती हैं और उन पर मतदान होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>लोकसभा</b> को <b>धन विधेयक (अनुच्छेद 110)</b> तथा <b>अनुदान एवं विनियोग</b> पर अनन्य नियंत्रण है, जबकि राज्यसभा केवल सिफारिश कर सकती है।<br>• <b>धन विधेयक</b> केवल लोकसभा में राष्ट्रपति की सिफारिश से पुरःस्थापित हो सकता है और राज्यसभा को इसे <b>14 दिन</b> में लौटाना होता है।<br>• मांगों पर मतदान के बाद <b>विनियोग विधेयक</b> अनुच्छेद <b>114</b> के अंतर्गत लाया जाता है, जो <b>भारत के समेकित निधि</b> से निकासी को प्राधिकृत करता है।<br>• लोकसभा में अनुदान मांग के विरुद्ध <b>कटौती प्रस्ताव</b> जैसे नीति कटौती, मितव्ययिता कटौती तथा प्रतीकात्मक कटौती प्रस्तुत की जा सकती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000071608","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Motion","question":{"en":"What physical quantity does an odometer measure in a vehicle? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वाहन में ओडोमीटर किस भौतिक राशि को मापता है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Speed of the vehicle","hi":"वाहन की चाल"},"2":{"en":"Distance travelled","hi":"तय की गई दूरी"},"3":{"en":"Time elapsed","hi":"बीता हुआ समय"},"4":{"en":"Acceleration rate","hi":"त्वरण की दर"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Distance travelled</b><br>An <b>odometer</b> measures the <b>total distance travelled</b> by a vehicle, while a <b>speedometer</b> shows its instantaneous speed.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The odometer reading is usually in <b>kilometres</b> and helps calculate mileage and servicing intervals.<br>• A <b>speedometer</b> measures speed in <b>km per hour</b> and works on the principle of the rotation of the wheels or a magnetic sensor.<br>• Distance is a <b>scalar</b> quantity, whereas <b>displacement</b> is a vector measured as the shortest path between two points.<br>• The <b>SI unit of distance</b> is the metre, and speed is distance divided by time with unit <b>metre per second</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – तय की गई दूरी</b><br><b>ओडोमीटर</b> वाहन द्वारा <b>तय की गई कुल दूरी</b> मापता है, जबकि <b>स्पीडोमीटर</b> उसकी तात्कालिक चाल दर्शाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ओडोमीटर का पाठ्यांक सामान्यतः <b>किलोमीटर</b> में होता है और इससे माइलेज तथा सर्विसिंग अंतराल ज्ञात किया जाता है।<br>• <b>स्पीडोमीटर</b> चाल <b>किमी प्रति घंटा</b> में मापता है और यह पहियों के घूर्णन अथवा चुंबकीय संवेदक के सिद्धांत पर कार्य करता है।<br>• दूरी <b>अदिश</b> राशि है, जबकि <b>विस्थापन</b> सदिश राशि है जो दो बिंदुओं के बीच न्यूनतम पथ होती है।<br>• <b>दूरी की SI इकाई</b> मीटर है तथा चाल दूरी को समय से भाग देकर प्राप्त होती है, जिसकी इकाई <b>मीटर प्रति सेकंड</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000071609","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Sound","question":{"en":"Which of the following is the frequency range of infrasonic sound waves? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी अवश्रव्य ध्वनि तरंगों की आवृत्ति सीमा है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Less than 10 Hertz only","hi":"केवल 10 हर्ट्ज़ से कम"},"2":{"en":"Less than 20 Hertz only","hi":"केवल 20 हर्ट्ज़ से कम"},"3":{"en":"Less than 30 Hertz only","hi":"केवल 30 हर्ट्ज़ से कम"},"4":{"en":"More than 20 Hertz only","hi":"केवल 20 हर्ट्ज़ से अधिक"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Less than 20 Hertz only</b><br><b>Infrasonic</b> sound waves have a frequency of <b>less than 20 Hz</b>, which is below the audible range of the human ear.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The human ear can hear sounds between <b>20 Hz and 20,000 Hz</b>, called the <b>audible range</b>.<br>• Sound above <b>20 kHz</b> is called <b>ultrasonic</b> and is used in <b>sonography, sonar and industrial testing</b>.<br>• Infrasonic waves are produced by <b>earthquakes, volcanoes, ocean waves and large animals</b> such as elephants and whales.<br>• Sound travels faster in <b>solids</b> than in liquids and gases, and its speed in air at room temperature is about <b>343 m/s</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – केवल 20 हर्ट्ज़ से कम</b><br><b>अवश्रव्य</b> ध्वनि तरंगों की आवृत्ति <b>20 हर्ट्ज़ से कम</b> होती है, जो मानव कान की श्रव्य सीमा से नीचे है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मानव कान <b>20 हर्ट्ज़ से 20,000 हर्ट्ज़</b> के बीच की ध्वनि सुन सकता है, जिसे <b>श्रव्य सीमा</b> कहते हैं।<br>• <b>20 किलोहर्ट्ज़</b> से अधिक की ध्वनि <b>पराश्रव्य</b> कहलाती है और इसका उपयोग <b>सोनोग्राफी, सोनार तथा औद्योगिक परीक्षण</b> में होता है।<br>• अवश्रव्य तरंगें <b>भूकंप, ज्वालामुखी, समुद्री लहरों</b> तथा हाथी एवं व्हेल जैसे बड़े जीवों द्वारा उत्पन्न होती हैं।<br>• ध्वनि <b>ठोसों</b> में द्रवों तथा गैसों की तुलना में अधिक तेज चलती है और कमरे के तापमान पर वायु में इसकी चाल लगभग <b>343 मीटर/सेकंड</b> होती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000071610","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Emergency & Constitutional Amendment","question":{"en":"Which constitutional amendment reduced the voting age in India from 21 years to 18 years? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किस संविधान संशोधन ने भारत में मतदान की आयु 21 वर्ष से घटाकर 18 वर्ष की? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"42nd Amendment","hi":"42वाँ संशोधन"},"2":{"en":"44th Amendment","hi":"44वाँ संशोधन"},"3":{"en":"61st Amendment","hi":"61वाँ संशोधन"},"4":{"en":"73rd Amendment","hi":"73वाँ संशोधन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 61st Amendment</b><br>The <b>61st Constitutional Amendment Act, 1988</b> reduced the voting age from <b>21 to 18 years</b> by amending <b>Article 326</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It came into force in <b>1989</b> and applies to elections to the <b>Lok Sabha and the State Legislative Assemblies</b>.<br>• <b>Article 326</b> provides for <b>adult suffrage</b>, that is, elections on the basis of one person, one vote for citizens above the prescribed age.<br>• The <b>42nd Amendment</b> is known as the Mini Constitution, the <b>44th Amendment</b> reversed several of its provisions and changed the emergency grounds.<br>• The <b>73rd Amendment</b> gave constitutional status to <b>Panchayati Raj</b> institutions and provided for reservation of seats.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 61वाँ संशोधन</b><br><b>61वें संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 1988</b> ने <b>अनुच्छेद 326</b> में संशोधन करके मतदान की आयु <b>21 से 18 वर्ष</b> कर दी।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह <b>1989</b> में प्रभावी हुआ और <b>लोकसभा तथा राज्य विधानसभाओं</b> के चुनावों पर लागू होता है।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 326</b> <b>वयस्क मताधिकार</b> का प्रावधान करता है, अर्थात् निर्धारित आयु से अधिक के नागरिकों को एक व्यक्ति एक वोट के आधार पर चुनाव का अधिकार।<br>• <b>42वाँ संशोधन</b> लघु संविधान कहलाता है, <b>44वाँ संशोधन</b> ने इसके कई प्रावधान बदले और आपातकाल के आधार में परिवर्तन किया।<br>• <b>73वें संशोधन</b> ने <b>पंचायती राज</b> संस्थाओं को संवैधानिक दर्जा दिया तथा सीटों के आरक्षण का प्रावधान किया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000071611","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Minerals","question":{"en":"Which district in Madhya Pradesh has important deposits of bauxite? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मध्य प्रदेश के किस जिले में बॉक्साइट के महत्वपूर्ण भंडार हैं? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Panna","hi":"पन्ना"},"2":{"en":"Katni","hi":"कटनी"},"3":{"en":"Jhabua","hi":"झाबुआ"},"4":{"en":"Indore","hi":"इंदौर"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Katni</b><br><b>Katni</b> district of Madhya Pradesh has important deposits of <b>bauxite</b>, the ore of aluminium.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Bauxite in Madhya Pradesh is found mainly in <b>Katni, Rewa, Satna, Shahdol and Mandla</b> districts.<br>• <b>Panna</b> is famous for <b>diamonds</b>, and <b>Jhabua</b> for <b>manganese</b> ore.<br>• Madhya Pradesh is rich in <b>manganese, coal, dolomite, limestone and bauxite</b>, and the state has major aluminium plants at <b>Korba and Singrauli</b> in the surrounding region.<br>• India's leading bauxite producing states are <b>Odisha, Gujarat, Maharashtra, Jharkhand and Chhattisgarh</b>, with major deposits at Panchpatmali and Amarkantak.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – कटनी</b><br>मध्य प्रदेश के <b>कटनी</b> जिले में एल्युमिनियम के अयस्क <b>बॉक्साइट</b> के महत्वपूर्ण भंडार हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मध्य प्रदेश में बॉक्साइट मुख्यतः <b>कटनी, रीवा, सतना, शहडोल तथा मंडला</b> जिलों में मिलता है।<br>• <b>पन्ना</b> <b>हीरे</b> के लिए तथा <b>झाबुआ</b> <b>मैंगनीज</b> अयस्क के लिए प्रसिद्ध है।<br>• मध्य प्रदेश <b>मैंगनीज, कोयला, डोलोमाइट, चूना पत्थर तथा बॉक्साइट</b> से समृद्ध है, और आसपास के क्षेत्र में <b>कोरबा एवं सिंगरौली</b> में प्रमुख एल्युमिनियम संयंत्र हैं।<br>• भारत के प्रमुख बॉक्साइट उत्पादक राज्य <b>ओडिशा, गुजरात, महाराष्ट्र, झारखंड तथा छत्तीसगढ़</b> हैं, जहाँ पंचपटमाली एवं अमरकंटक में बड़े भंडार हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000071612","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"What was the total number of medals won by India at the Paris 2024 Summer Olympics? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"पेरिस 2024 ग्रीष्मकालीन ओलंपिक में भारत ने कुल कितने पदक जीते? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5 medals","hi":"5 पदक"},"2":{"en":"6 medals","hi":"6 पदक"},"3":{"en":"7 medals","hi":"7 पदक"},"4":{"en":"10 medals","hi":"10 पदक"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 6 medals</b><br>India won <b>6 medals</b> at the <b>Paris 2024 Olympics</b> - <b>1 silver and 5 bronze</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Neeraj Chopra</b> won <b>silver</b> in javelin throw, and <b>Manu Bhaker</b> won two bronze medals in shooting.<br>• Other bronze medallists were the <b>men's hockey team, Swapnil Kusale</b> in shooting and <b>Aman Sehrawat</b> in wrestling.<br>• India's highest medal tally remains <b>7 medals at Tokyo 2020</b>, and its first participation was in <b>1900 Paris</b> through Norman Pritchard.<br>• The <b>Paris 2024</b> Games saw <b>206 National Olympic Committees</b> participate, and the next Summer Olympics will be held in <b>Los Angeles in 2028</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 6 पदक</b><br>भारत ने <b>पेरिस 2024 ओलंपिक</b> में <b>6 पदक</b> - <b>1 रजत तथा 5 कांस्य</b> - जीते।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>नीरज चोपड़ा</b> ने भाला फेंक में <b>रजत</b> जीता तथा <b>मनु भाकर</b> ने निशानेबाजी में दो कांस्य पदक जीते।<br>• अन्य कांस्य पदक विजेता <b>पुरुष हॉकी टीम, निशानेबाजी में स्वप्निल कुसाले</b> तथा कुश्ती में <b>अमन सहरावत</b> रहे।<br>• भारत का सर्वाधिक पदक रिकॉर्ड <b>टोक्यो 2020 में 7 पदक</b> है, तथा पहली भागीदारी <b>1900 पेरिस</b> में नॉर्मन प्रिचर्ड के माध्यम से हुई।<br>• <b>पेरिस 2024</b> में <b>206 राष्ट्रीय ओलंपिक समितियों</b> ने भाग लिया तथा अगला ग्रीष्मकालीन ओलंपिक <b>2028 में लॉस एंजिलिस</b> में होगा।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000071613","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which Indian badminton pair won the country's first-ever Asian Games gold medal in badminton at the 2022 Asian Games? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"2022 एशियाई खेलों में किस भारतीय बैडमिंटन युग्म ने बैडमिंटन में देश का पहला एशियाई खेल स्वर्ण पदक जीता? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PV Sindhu and Saina Nehwal","hi":"पी.वी. सिंधु तथा साइना नेहवाल"},"2":{"en":"Satwiksairaj Rankireddy and Chirag Shetty","hi":"सात्विकसाईराज रंकीरेड्डी तथा चिराग शेट्टी"},"3":{"en":"Lakshya Sen and HS Prannoy","hi":"लक्ष्य सेन तथा एच.एस. प्रणय"},"4":{"en":"Jwala Gutta and Ashwini Ponnappa","hi":"ज्वाला गुट्टा तथा अश्विनी पोनप्पा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Satwiksairaj Rankireddy and Chirag Shetty</b><br><b>Satwiksairaj Rankireddy</b> and <b>Chirag Shetty</b> won the <b>men's doubles gold</b> at the <b>2022 Asian Games</b> held in Hangzhou, India's first Asian Games gold in badminton.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The pair is known as the <b>\"Sat-Chi\"</b> combination and has also won medals at the <b>World Championships</b> and the <b>Thomas Cup</b>.<br>• India won its first <b>Thomas Cup title in 2022</b>, with the pair playing a key role.<br>• <b>P.V. Sindhu</b> won a silver at the 2016 Olympics and bronze at Tokyo 2020, and <b>Saina Nehwal</b> won bronze at London 2012.<br>• The <b>2022 Asian Games</b> were held in <b>Hangzhou, China</b>, in 2023 because of the pandemic, and India finished fourth in the medal tally.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सात्विकसाईराज रंकीरेड्डी तथा चिराग शेट्टी</b><br><b>सात्विकसाईराज रंकीरेड्डी</b> तथा <b>चिराग शेट्टी</b> ने हांगझोऊ में आयोजित <b>2022 एशियाई खेलों</b> में <b>पुरुष युगल स्वर्ण</b> जीता, जो बैडमिंटन में भारत का पहला एशियाई खेल स्वर्ण था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इस युग्म को <b>\"सैट-ची\"</b> कहा जाता है और इसने <b>विश्व चैंपियनशिप</b> तथा <b>थॉमस कप</b> में भी पदक जीते हैं।<br>• भारत ने <b>2022 में पहला थॉमस कप खिताब</b> जीता, जिसमें इस युग्म की प्रमुख भूमिका थी।<br>• <b>पी.वी. सिंधु</b> ने 2016 ओलंपिक में रजत तथा टोक्यो 2020 में कांस्य जीता, और <b>साइना नेहवाल</b> ने लंदन 2012 में कांस्य जीता।<br>• <b>2022 एशियाई खेल</b> महामारी के कारण 2023 में <b>हांगझोऊ, चीन</b> में हुए, जहाँ भारत पदक तालिका में चौथे स्थान पर रहा।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000071614","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Awards and Honours (Current)","question":{"en":"Gokul Chandra Das, who received the Padma Shri in 2025, is renowned for his mastery of which traditional Bengali percussion instrument? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"2025 में पद्म श्री प्राप्त करने वाले गोकुल चंद्र दास किस पारंपरिक बंगाली ताल वाद्य में अपनी निपुणता के लिए प्रसिद्ध हैं? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tabla","hi":"तबला"},"2":{"en":"Dhak","hi":"ढाक"},"3":{"en":"Shehnai","hi":"शहनाई"},"4":{"en":"Sitar","hi":"सितार"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Dhak</b><br><b>Gokul Chandra Das</b> was awarded the <b>Padma Shri in 2025</b> for his mastery of the <b>dhak</b>, the traditional Bengali drum played during <b>Durga Puja</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>dhak</b> is a large <b>double-headed drum</b> played with sticks, and its sound is central to the <b>agomoni and bijoya</b> celebrations of Durga Puja.<br>• Dhak players are called <b>dhakis</b> and traditionally travel to towns during the festival season.<br>• The <b>Padma Shri</b> is announced on the eve of <b>Republic Day</b> and honours distinguished service in various fields.<br>• Other Bengali instruments include the <b>khol</b> used in kirtan, the <b>ektara</b> of the Bauls and the <b>dotara</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – ढाक</b><br><b>गोकुल चंद्र दास</b> को <b>2025 में पद्म श्री</b> <b>ढाक</b> में निपुणता के लिए दिया गया, जो <b>दुर्गा पूजा</b> के समय बजाया जाने वाला पारंपरिक बंगाली ढोल है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>ढाक</b> एक बड़ा <b>दोनों ओर मुख वाला ढोल</b> है जिसे डंडियों से बजाया जाता है और इसकी ध्वनि दुर्गा पूजा के <b>आगमनी तथा विजया</b> उत्सव का केंद्र होती है।<br>• ढाक बजाने वालों को <b>ढाकी</b> कहा जाता है और वे परंपरागत रूप से उत्सव के समय नगरों में आते हैं।<br>• <b>पद्म श्री</b> की घोषणा <b>गणतंत्र दिवस</b> की पूर्व संध्या पर होती है और यह विविध क्षेत्रों में विशिष्ट सेवा के लिए दिया जाता है।<br>• अन्य बंगाली वाद्यों में कीर्तन का <b>खोल</b>, बाउलों का <b>एकतारा</b> तथा <b>दोतारा</b> शामिल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000071615","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who assumed office as the 26th Chief Election Commissioner of India on 19 February 2025? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"19 फरवरी 2025 को भारत के 26वें मुख्य निर्वाचन आयुक्त के रूप में किसने पदभार संभाला? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rajiv Kumar","hi":"राजीव कुमार"},"2":{"en":"Gyanesh Kumar","hi":"ज्ञानेश कुमार"},"3":{"en":"Sukhbir Singh Sandhu","hi":"सुखबीर सिंह संधू"},"4":{"en":"Anup Chandra Pandey","hi":"अनूप चंद्र पांडेय"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Gyanesh Kumar</b><br><b>Gyanesh Kumar</b> assumed office as the <b>26th Chief Election Commissioner</b> of India on <b>19 February 2025</b>, succeeding <b>Rajiv Kumar</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• He is a former <b>IAS officer of the Kerala cadre</b> and served as <b>Election Commissioner</b> before his appointment as CEC.<br>• His appointment was made under the <b>CEC and Other Election Commissioners (Appointment, Conditions of Service and Term of Office) Act, 2023</b>.<br>• The selection committee consists of the <b>Prime Minister, a Union Cabinet Minister and the Leader of the Opposition in the Lok Sabha</b>.<br>• <b>Sukhbir Singh Sandhu</b> and <b>Anup Chandra Pandey</b> are former Election Commissioners, and the <b>Election Commission</b> functions under <b>Article 324</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – ज्ञानेश कुमार</b><br><b>ज्ञानेश कुमार</b> ने <b>19 फरवरी 2025</b> को <b>राजीव कुमार</b> के स्थान पर भारत के <b>26वें मुख्य निर्वाचन आयुक्त</b> के रूप में पदभार संभाला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वे <b>केरल कैडर</b> के पूर्व <b>आईएएस अधिकारी</b> हैं और CEC बनने से पहले <b>निर्वाचन आयुक्त</b> रहे।<br>• उनकी नियुक्ति <b>CEC तथा अन्य निर्वाचन आयुक्त (नियुक्ति, सेवा शर्तें तथा कार्यकाल) अधिनियम, 2023</b> के अंतर्गत हुई।<br>• चयन समिति में <b>प्रधानमंत्री, एक केंद्रीय मंत्रिमंडल मंत्री तथा लोकसभा में विपक्ष के नेता</b> होते हैं।<br>• <b>सुखबीर सिंह संधू</b> तथा <b>अनूप चंद्र पांडेय</b> पूर्व निर्वाचन आयुक्त हैं, और <b>निर्वाचन आयोग</b> <b>अनुच्छेद 324</b> के अंतर्गत कार्य करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000071616","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"Why is the Hornbill Festival known as the \"Festival of Festivals\"? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"हॉर्नबिल महोत्सव को \"महोत्सवों का महोत्सव\" क्यों कहा जाता है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It showcases all Naga tribes in one place","hi":"यह सभी नागा जनजातियों को एक स्थान पर प्रदर्शित करता है"},"2":{"en":"It attracts global music artists","hi":"यह वैश्विक संगीत कलाकारों को आकर्षित करता है"},"3":{"en":"It celebrates the regional winter harvest","hi":"यह क्षेत्रीय शीतकालीन फसल का उत्सव है"},"4":{"en":"It promotes modern state industries","hi":"यह आधुनिक राज्य उद्योगों को बढ़ावा देता है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – It showcases all Naga tribes in one place</b><br>The <b>Hornbill Festival</b> is called the <b>\"Festival of Festivals\"</b> because it brings together <b>all the Naga tribes</b> at one place, displaying their dances, music, crafts and food.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It is celebrated from <b>1 to 10 December</b> every year at <b>Kisama Heritage Village</b> near Kohima, Nagaland.<br>• The festival is named after the <b>Hornbill bird</b>, which is revered in Naga culture and features in their folklore and headgear.<br>• It was started in <b>2000</b> by the Government of Nagaland to promote <b>tribal unity and tourism</b>.<br>• Other major northeastern festivals are <b>Bihu (Assam), Wangala (Meghalaya), Sangai (Manipur) and Ziro Music Festival (Arunachal Pradesh)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – यह सभी नागा जनजातियों को एक स्थान पर प्रदर्शित करता है</b><br><b>हॉर्नबिल महोत्सव</b> को <b>\"महोत्सवों का महोत्सव\"</b> कहा जाता है क्योंकि यह <b>सभी नागा जनजातियों</b> को एक स्थान पर लाकर उनके नृत्य, संगीत, शिल्प तथा भोजन का प्रदर्शन करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह प्रतिवर्ष <b>1 से 10 दिसंबर</b> तक नगालैंड में कोहिमा के निकट <b>किसामा हेरिटेज विलेज</b> में मनाया जाता है।<br>• इसका नाम <b>हॉर्नबिल पक्षी</b> पर है, जो नागा संस्कृति में पूज्य है और उनकी लोककथाओं तथा शिरोभूषा में दिखता है।<br>• इसे <b>2000</b> में नगालैंड सरकार ने <b>जनजातीय एकता तथा पर्यटन</b> को बढ़ावा देने के लिए आरंभ किया।<br>• पूर्वोत्तर के अन्य प्रमुख उत्सव <b>बिहू (असम), वांगला (मेघालय), संगाई (मणिपुर) तथा जीरो संगीत महोत्सव (अरुणाचल प्रदेश)</b> हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000071617","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Vedic Age","question":{"en":"Which feature most clearly reflects the shared Indo-European cultural tradition? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कौन-सी विशेषता साझा भारत-यूरोपीय सांस्कृतिक परंपरा को सर्वाधिक स्पष्ट रूप से दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Fire and soma cults","hi":"अग्नि तथा सोम पूजा"},"2":{"en":"Iron city fortifications","hi":"लोहे के नगर दुर्ग"},"3":{"en":"Temple-based worship","hi":"मंदिर आधारित पूजा"},"4":{"en":"Maritime trade routes","hi":"समुद्री व्यापार मार्ग"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Fire and soma cults</b><br>The <b>fire cult</b> and the <b>soma ritual</b> are shared features of the <b>Indo-European</b> religious tradition, appearing in the <b>Rigveda</b> and in ancient Iranian and European traditions.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Rigveda</b> devotes many hymns to <b>Agni</b>, the fire god, and the fire sacrifice (<b>yajna</b>) became central to Vedic religion.<br>• <b>Soma</b> was a sacred drink offered to the gods, corresponding to the <b>haoma</b> ritual of ancient Iran, showing a common origin.<br>• The <b>Indo-European language family</b> links Sanskrit with Greek, Latin and Persian, and scholars such as <b>William Jones</b> noted these similarities.<br>• Temple-based worship developed later in India, and iron fortifications and maritime routes are not markers of Indo-European culture.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – अग्नि तथा सोम पूजा</b><br><b>अग्नि पूजा</b> तथा <b>सोम संस्कार</b> <b>भारत-यूरोपीय</b> धार्मिक परंपरा की साझा विशेषताएँ हैं, जो <b>ऋग्वेद</b> तथा प्राचीन ईरानी एवं यूरोपीय परंपराओं में मिलती हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>ऋग्वेद</b> में अग्नि देवता के लिए अनेक सूक्त हैं और <b>यज्ञ</b> वैदिक धर्म का केंद्र बन गया।<br>• <b>सोम</b> देवताओं को अर्पित पवित्र पेय था, जो प्राचीन ईरान के <b>होम</b> संस्कार से मेल खाता है और साझा उद्गम दर्शाता है।<br>• <b>भारत-यूरोपीय भाषा परिवार</b> संस्कृत को यूनानी, लातीनी तथा फारसी से जोड़ता है, तथा <b>विलियम जोन्स</b> जैसे विद्वानों ने इन समानताओं को रेखांकित किया।<br>• मंदिर आधारित पूजा भारत में बाद में विकसित हुई, तथा लौह दुर्ग एवं समुद्री मार्ग भारत-यूरोपीय संस्कृति के लक्षण नहीं हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000071618","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"What is the main focus of the Amrit Bharat Station Scheme introduced by the Ministry of Railways, Government of India? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत सरकार के रेल मंत्रालय द्वारा शुरू की गई अमृत भारत स्टेशन योजना का मुख्य फोकस क्या है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Building new high-speed rail corridors","hi":"नए उच्च गति रेल गलियारे बनाना"},"2":{"en":"Continuous development of railway stations with a long-term vision","hi":"दीर्घकालिक दृष्टि से रेलवे स्टेशनों का सतत विकास"},"3":{"en":"Privatization of all premium trains","hi":"सभी प्रीमियम ट्रेनों का निजीकरण"},"4":{"en":"Providing free Wi-Fi in 100% of rural stations","hi":"100% ग्रामीण स्टेशनों में निःशुल्क वाई-फाई प्रदान करना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Continuous development of railway stations with a long-term vision</b><br>The <b>Amrit Bharat Station Scheme</b> focuses on the <b>continuous development of railway stations</b> with a <b>long-term vision</b>, preparing master plans for stations and upgrading them in phases.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Launched in <b>2023</b>, the scheme aims to modernise more than <b>1,300 railway stations</b> across the country.<br>• Improvements include <b>better station buildings and circulating areas, improved amenities, lifts and escalators, signage, divyang-friendly facilities and rooftop solar</b>.<br>• It is implemented by the <b>Ministry of Railways</b> through the <b>Rail Land Development Authority</b> and zonal railways.<br>• Related initiatives include <b>Kavach</b> for train safety, <b>dedicated freight corridors</b> and the <b>station redevelopment programme</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – दीर्घकालिक दृष्टि से रेलवे स्टेशनों का सतत विकास</b><br><b>अमृत भारत स्टेशन योजना</b> <b>दीर्घकालिक दृष्टि</b> से <b>रेलवे स्टेशनों के सतत विकास</b> पर केंद्रित है और स्टेशनों के मास्टर प्लान बनाकर उन्हें चरणबद्ध रूप से उन्नत किया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>2023</b> में शुरू इस योजना का लक्ष्य देश भर के <b>1,300 से अधिक रेलवे स्टेशनों</b> का आधुनिकीकरण है।<br>• सुधारों में <b>बेहतर स्टेशन भवन तथा परिसंचरण क्षेत्र, बेहतर सुविधाएँ, लिफ्ट एवं एस्केलेटर, साइनेज, दिव्यांग-अनुकूल सुविधाएँ तथा छत पर सौर ऊर्जा</b> शामिल हैं।<br>• इसे <b>रेल मंत्रालय</b> <b>रेल भूमि विकास प्राधिकरण</b> तथा क्षेत्रीय रेलवे के माध्यम से क्रियान्वित करता है।<br>• संबंधित पहलों में ट्रेन सुरक्षा हेतु <b>कवच</b>, <b>समर्पित माल गलियारे</b> तथा <b>स्टेशन पुनर्विकास कार्यक्रम</b> शामिल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000071619","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"What is the present name of the Mid-Day Meal Scheme in India (2026)? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में मध्याह्न भोजन योजना का वर्तमान नाम (2026) क्या है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"National School Nutrition Programme (NSNP)","hi":"राष्ट्रीय विद्यालय पोषण कार्यक्रम (NSNP)"},"2":{"en":"PM POSHAN (Pradhan Mantri Poshan Shakti Nirman)","hi":"पीएम पोषण (प्रधानमंत्री पोषण शक्ति निर्माण)"},"3":{"en":"Pradhan Mantri Annapurna Yojana (PMAY)","hi":"प्रधानमंत्री अन्नपूर्णा योजना (PMAY)"},"4":{"en":"Pradhan Mantri Shakti Aahar Yojana (PM-Shakti Aahar Yojana)","hi":"प्रधानमंत्री शक्ति आहार योजना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – PM POSHAN (Pradhan Mantri Poshan Shakti Nirman)</b><br>The <b>Mid-Day Meal Scheme</b> was renamed <b>PM POSHAN</b> (Pradhan Mantri Poshan Shakti Nirman) in <b>2021</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• PM POSHAN covers students of <b>Classes I to VIII</b> in government and government-aided schools and also children in <b>Balvatika</b>.<br>• The scheme aims to improve <b>nutritional standards</b> of school children and encourage <b>regular attendance</b>.<br>• It also includes <b>supplementary nutrition for pregnant women and lactating mothers</b> in aspirational districts.<br>• The scheme is implemented by the <b>Ministry of Education</b> and involves <b>school management committees</b> and local bodies.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पीएम पोषण (प्रधानमंत्री पोषण शक्ति निर्माण)</b><br><b>मध्याह्न भोजन योजना</b> का नाम <b>2021</b> में बदलकर <b>पीएम पोषण</b> (प्रधानमंत्री पोषण शक्ति निर्माण) कर दिया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पीएम पोषण सरकारी तथा सरकारी सहायता प्राप्त विद्यालयों के <b>कक्षा I से VIII</b> के विद्यार्थियों तथा <b>बालवाटिका</b> के बच्चों को सम्मिलित करता है।<br>• योजना का उद्देश्य विद्यार्थियों के <b>पोषण स्तर</b> में सुधार तथा <b>नियमित उपस्थिति</b> को प्रोत्साहित करना है।<br>• इसमें आकांक्षी जिलों में <b>गर्भवती महिलाओं तथा स्तनपान कराने वाली माताओं</b> को पूरक पोषण भी शामिल है।<br>• योजना <b>शिक्षा मंत्रालय</b> द्वारा क्रियान्वित होती है, जिसमें <b>विद्यालय प्रबंधन समितियाँ</b> तथा स्थानीय निकाय भागीदार होते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000071620","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: International News","question":{"en":"The proposal for conducting trade in national currencies among BRICS (Brazil, Russia, India, China, and South Africa) countries primarily seeks to reduce dependence on the: [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"ब्रिक्स (ब्राजील, रूस, भारत, चीन तथा दक्षिण अफ्रीका) देशों के बीच राष्ट्रीय मुद्राओं में व्यापार करने का प्रस्ताव मुख्यतः किस पर निर्भरता घटाना चाहता है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Europe Euro","hi":"यूरो"},"2":{"en":"Japanese Yen","hi":"जापानी येन"},"3":{"en":"United States Dollar","hi":"अमेरिकी डॉलर"},"4":{"en":"British Pound Sterling","hi":"ब्रिटिश पाउंड स्टर्लिंग"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – United States Dollar</b><br>Trading in <b>national currencies</b> among BRICS countries aims mainly at reducing dependence on the <b>United States dollar</b>, which dominates global trade and payments.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A large share of global trade is invoiced in dollars, so countries hold dollar reserves and are exposed to <b>exchange rate risk and sanctions</b>.<br>• BRICS has promoted <b>local currency settlement, the New Development Bank and the Contingent Reserve Arrangement</b> to reduce this dependence.<br>• The <b>2023 Johannesburg summit</b> and later summits discussed trade in local currencies and alternative payment systems.<br>• India has supported <b>rupee trade settlement</b> arrangements with several countries to reduce dollar reliance in bilateral trade.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अमेरिकी डॉलर</b><br>ब्रिक्स देशों के बीच <b>राष्ट्रीय मुद्राओं</b> में व्यापार का उद्देश्य मुख्यतः <b>अमेरिकी डॉलर</b> पर निर्भरता घटाना है, जो वैश्विक व्यापार तथा भुगतान में प्रभुत्व रखता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वैश्विक व्यापार का बड़ा भाग डॉलर में ही होता है, अतः देशों को डॉलर भंडार रखना पड़ता है और वे <b>विनिमय दर जोखिम तथा प्रतिबंधों</b> के प्रति उजागर होते हैं।<br>• ब्रिक्स ने इस निर्भरता को घटाने के लिए <b>स्थानीय मुद्रा निपटान, नई विकास बैंक तथा आकस्मिक आरक्षित व्यवस्था</b> को बढ़ावा दिया है।<br>• <b>जोहान्सबर्ग 2023 शिखर सम्मेलन</b> तथा बाद के सम्मेलनों में स्थानीय मुद्राओं में व्यापार तथा वैकल्पिक भुगतान प्रणालियों पर चर्चा हुई।<br>• भारत ने द्विपक्षीय व्यापार में डॉलर पर निर्भरता घटाने हेतु कई देशों के साथ <b>रुपया व्यापार निपटान</b> व्यवस्था का समर्थन किया है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000071621","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"Under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 in India, which of the following correctly distinguishes \"dishonestly\" from \"fraudulently\"? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 के अंतर्गत निम्नलिखित में से कौन \"बेईमानी से\" तथा \"कपटपूर्ण\" में सही अंतर स्पष्ट करता है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\"Dishonestly\" requires deception, while \"fraudulently\" requires wrongful gain or loss.","hi":"\"बेईमानी से\" में छल आवश्यक है, जबकि \"कपटपूर्ण\" में अनुचित लाभ अथवा हानि आवश्यक है।"},"2":{"en":"\"Fraudulently\" requires intention to defraud, while \"dishonestly\" concerns wrongful gain or wrongful loss.","hi":"\"कपटपूर्ण\" में ठगने का आशय आवश्यक है, जबकि \"बेईमानी से\" अनुचित लाभ अथवा अनुचित हानि से संबंधित है।"},"3":{"en":"Both terms are legally identical in all contexts.","hi":"दोनों शब्द सभी संदर्भों में विधिक रूप से समान हैं।"},"4":{"en":"\"Fraudulently\" applies only to property offences, while \"dishonestly\" applies only to bodily offences.","hi":"\"कपटपूर्ण\" केवल संपत्ति अपराधों पर तथा \"बेईमानी से\" केवल शारीरिक अपराधों पर लागू होता है।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – \"Fraudulently\" requires intention to defraud, while \"dishonestly\" concerns wrongful gain or wrongful loss</b><br>Under the <b>Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023</b>, <b>\"fraudulently\"</b> refers to an act done with the <b>intention to defraud</b>, while <b>\"dishonestly\"</b> refers to an act done with the intention of causing <b>wrongful gain or wrongful loss</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Wrongful gain</b> means gain of property by unlawful means, and <b>wrongful loss</b> means loss of property by unlawful means.<br>• <b>Fraudulently</b> involves <b>deception</b> and an intention to induce a person to part with property or a right.<br>• These definitions appear in the <b>general explanations</b> of the BNS and are used in offences such as <b>cheating, criminal breach of trust and forgery</b>.<br>• The BNS replaced the <b>Indian Penal Code, 1860</b> and came into force on <b>1 July 2024</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – \"कपटपूर्ण\" में ठगने का आशय आवश्यक है, जबकि \"बेईमानी से\" अनुचित लाभ अथवा अनुचित हानि से संबंधित है।</b><br><b>भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023</b> के अंतर्गत <b>\"कपटपूर्ण\"</b> का अर्थ <b>ठगने के आशय</b> से किया गया कार्य है, जबकि <b>\"बेईमानी से\"</b> का अर्थ <b>अनुचित लाभ अथवा अनुचित हानि</b> करने के आशय से किया गया कार्य है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनुचित लाभ</b> का अर्थ अवैध साधनों से संपत्ति का लाभ तथा <b>अनुचित हानि</b> का अर्थ अवैध साधनों से संपत्ति की हानि है।<br>• <b>कपटपूर्ण</b> में <b>छल</b> तथा किसी व्यक्ति को संपत्ति अथवा अधिकार छोड़ने के लिए प्रेरित करने का आशय सम्मिलित होता है।<br>• ये परिभाषाएँ BNS के <b>सामान्य व्याख्या</b> भाग में हैं और <b>ठगी, आपराधिक न्यासभंग तथा कूटरचना</b> जैसे अपराधों में प्रयुक्त होती हैं।<br>• BNS ने <b>भारतीय दंड संहिता, 1860</b> का स्थान लिया और यह <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से प्रभावी हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000071622","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A statute declares that registration of a document shall be \"conclusive proof\" of its execution. During trial, the opposing party seeks to adduce oral evidence denying execution despite the document being duly registered. What should the court do under the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक विधि घोषित करती है कि दस्तावेज़ का पंजीकरण उसके निष्पादन का \"निर्णायक प्रमाण\" होगा। विचारण के दौरान विरोधी पक्ष दस्तावेज़ के विधिवत पंजीकृत होने के बावजूद निष्पादन से इनकार करते हुए मौखिक साक्ष्य प्रस्तुत करना चाहता है। भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 2023 के अंतर्गत न्यायालय को क्या करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Allow rebuttal because every presumption is rebuttable.","hi":"खंडन की अनुमति दें क्योंकि प्रत्येक उपधारणा खंडनीय होती है।"},"2":{"en":"Reject the evidence because conclusive proof bars disproving evidence.","hi":"साक्ष्य अस्वीकार करें क्योंकि निर्णायक प्रमाण विरोधी साक्ष्य को वर्जित करता है।"},"3":{"en":"Treat the matter as merely \"may presume.\"","hi":"मामले को केवल \"उपधारणा कर सकता है\" मानें।"},"4":{"en":"Permit rebuttal only through documentary evidence.","hi":"खंडन केवल दस्तावेज़ी साक्ष्य से अनुमत करें।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Reject the evidence because conclusive proof bars disproving evidence</b><br>Where a law declares a fact to be <b>\"conclusive proof\"</b>, the court must treat the fact as proved and <b>cannot allow evidence to disprove it</b>, so the oral evidence denying execution should be rejected.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023</b> classifies presumptions as <b>\"may presume\", \"shall presume\"</b> and <b>\"conclusive proof\"</b>.<br>• <b>\"May presume\"</b> is a discretionary presumption that the court may draw or call for proof, while <b>\"shall presume\"</b> is obligatory but rebuttable.<br>• <b>Conclusive proof</b> is an irrebuttable presumption, and no evidence is allowed to contradict the fact so declared.<br>• The BSA replaced the <b>Indian Evidence Act, 1872</b> and came into force on <b>1 July 2024</b>, giving greater scope to <b>electronic and digital evidence</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – साक्ष्य अस्वीकार करें क्योंकि निर्णायक प्रमाण विरोधी साक्ष्य को वर्जित करता है।</b><br>जहाँ विधि किसी तथ्य को <b>\"निर्णायक प्रमाण\"</b> घोषित करती है, वहाँ न्यायालय को उस तथ्य को सिद्ध मानना होता है और <b>उसके विरुद्ध साक्ष्य की अनुमति नहीं दी जा सकती</b>, अतः निष्पादन से इनकार करने वाला मौखिक साक्ष्य अस्वीकार किया जाना चाहिए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 2023</b> उपधारणाओं को <b>\"उपधारणा कर सकता है\", \"उपधारणा करेगा\"</b> तथा <b>\"निर्णायक प्रमाण\"</b> में वर्गीकृत करता है।<br>• <b>\"उपधारणा कर सकता है\"</b> विवेकाधीन उपधारणा है जिसे न्यायालय ग्रहण कर सकता है अथवा प्रमाण मांग सकता है, जबकि <b>\"उपधारणा करेगा\"</b> अनिवार्य परंतु खंडनीय है।<br>• <b>निर्णायक प्रमाण</b> अखंडनीय उपधारणा है और इस प्रकार घोषित तथ्य के विरुद्ध कोई साक्ष्य अनुमत नहीं होता।<br>• BSA ने <b>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 1872</b> का स्थान लिया और <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से प्रभावी हुआ, जिसमें <b>इलेक्ट्रॉनिक तथा डिजिटल साक्ष्य</b> को अधिक स्थान मिला।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000071623","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: International News","question":{"en":"Which country conferred its highest civilian honor, the \"Mitra Vibhushana,\" on Prime Minister Narendra Modi in 2025? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किस देश ने 2025 में प्रधानमंत्री नरेंद्र मोदी को अपना सर्वोच्च नागरिक सम्मान \"मित्र विभूषण\" प्रदान किया? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Nepal","hi":"नेपाल"},"2":{"en":"Sri Lanka","hi":"श्रीलंका"},"3":{"en":"Bangladesh","hi":"बांग्लादेश"},"4":{"en":"Bhutan","hi":"भूटान"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Sri Lanka</b><br><b>Sri Lanka</b> conferred its highest civilian honour, the <b>Mitra Vibhushana</b>, on Prime Minister <b>Narendra Modi</b> in <b>2025</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Sri Lanka</b> is India's closest maritime neighbour and a key partner under the <b>Neighbourhood First</b> policy and <b>SAGAR</b> vision.<br>• India has supported Sri Lanka through <b>credit lines, currency support and development projects</b>, including in energy and connectivity.<br>• Sri Lanka's highest civilian honour is the <b>Sri Lankabhimanya</b>, and the <b>Mitra Vibhushana</b> is awarded for exceptional service to the nation and to bilateral friendship.<br>• <b>Nepal</b> conferred the <b>Order of the Ojaswi Rajanya</b> on Indian leaders, and <b>Bhutan</b> awards the <b>Order of the Druk Gyalpo</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – श्रीलंका</b><br><b>श्रीलंका</b> ने <b>2025</b> में प्रधानमंत्री <b>नरेंद्र मोदी</b> को अपना सर्वोच्च नागरिक सम्मान <b>मित्र विभूषण</b> प्रदान किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>श्रीलंका</b> भारत का निकटतम समुद्री पड़ोसी है तथा <b>पड़ोसी प्रथम</b> नीति एवं <b>सागर</b> दृष्टि के अंतर्गत प्रमुख साझेदार है।<br>• भारत ने <b>ऋण सीमाओं, मुद्रा सहायता तथा विकास परियोजनाओं</b> के माध्यम से श्रीलंका की सहायता की है, जिसमें ऊर्जा तथा संयोजकता भी शामिल है।<br>• श्रीलंका का सर्वोच्च नागरिक सम्मान <b>श्री लंकाभिमान्य</b> है, तथा <b>मित्र विभूषण</b> राष्ट्र तथा द्विपक्षीय मैत्री की विशिष्ट सेवा के लिए दिया जाता है।<br>• <b>नेपाल</b> ने भारतीय नेताओं को <b>ओजस्वी राजन्य</b> तथा <b>भूटान</b> <b>ड्रुक ग्यालपो</b> सम्मान प्रदान करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000071624","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: National Parks","question":{"en":"Kuno National Park, which was visited by the President of India, Droupadi Murmu, in June 2026, is located in which state? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कुनो राष्ट्रीय उद्यान, जिसका दौरा भारत की राष्ट्रपति द्रौपदी मुर्मू ने जून 2026 में किया, किस राज्य में स्थित है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rajasthan","hi":"राजस्थान"},"2":{"en":"Madhya Pradesh","hi":"मध्य प्रदेश"},"3":{"en":"Andhra Pradesh","hi":"आंध्र प्रदेश"},"4":{"en":"Maharashtra","hi":"महाराष्ट्र"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Madhya Pradesh</b><br><b>Kuno National Park</b> is located in <b>Sheopur district of Madhya Pradesh</b> and is famous for its <b>Asiatic lion relocation project</b> and reintroduced <b>cheetahs</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Kuno was declared a <b>national park in 2018</b> and is part of the <b>Sheopur-Shivpuri dry deciduous forest</b> landscape in the Vindhyan ranges.<br>• In <b>September 2022</b>, cheetahs from <b>Namibia</b> were introduced at Kuno under <b>Project Cheetah</b>, the first intercontinental translocation of the species to India.<br>• The park is drained by the <b>Kuno river</b>, a tributary of the Chambal, and has <b>grassland and scrub forest</b> habitat suited to cheetahs.<br>• Other famous national parks include <b>Gir (Gujarat) for Asiatic lions, Kaziranga (Assam) for one-horned rhinos and Jim Corbett (Uttarakhand)</b>, India's oldest national park.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मध्य प्रदेश</b><br><b>कुनो राष्ट्रीय उद्यान</b> <b>मध्य प्रदेश के श्योपुर जिले</b> में स्थित है और यह <b>एशियाई सिंह पुनर्वास परियोजना</b> तथा पुनःस्थापित <b>चीतों</b> के लिए प्रसिद्ध है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• कुनो को <b>2018</b> में राष्ट्रीय उद्यान घोषित किया गया और यह विंध्य श्रेणी के <b>श्योपुर-शिवपुरी शुष्क पर्णपाती वन</b> परिदृश्य का भाग है।<br>• <b>सितंबर 2022</b> में <b>नामीबिया</b> से चीते <b>प्रोजेक्ट चीता</b> के अंतर्गत कुनो लाए गए, जो भारत में इस प्रजाति का पहला अंतरमहाद्वीपीय स्थानांतरण था।<br>• उद्यान <b>कुनो नदी</b> से अपवाहित होता है, जो चंबल की सहायक है, तथा यहाँ चीतों के अनुकूल <b>घास के मैदान एवं झाड़ी वन</b> आवास हैं।<br>• अन्य प्रसिद्ध राष्ट्रीय उद्यानों में <b>गिर (गुजरात) एशियाई सिंहों के लिए, काजीरंगा (असम) एक सींग वाले गैंडों के लिए तथा जिम कॉर्बेट (उत्तराखंड)</b>, जो भारत का सबसे पुराना राष्ट्रीय उद्यान है, शामिल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000071625","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Why were higher domestic saving and investment rates important for India's economic growth after the 1991 reforms? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"1991 के सुधारों के बाद भारत के आर्थिक विकास के लिए उच्च घरेलू बचत तथा निवेश दरें क्यों महत्वपूर्ण थीं? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They increase fiscal deficits and weaken financial stability","hi":"वे राजकोषीय घाटा बढ़ाती हैं तथा वित्तीय स्थिरता कमजोर करती हैं"},"2":{"en":"They discourage entrepreneurship and limit business expansion","hi":"वे उद्यमशीलता को हतोत्साहित करती हैं तथा व्यापार विस्तार सीमित करती हैं"},"3":{"en":"They enhance capital formation and long-term growth potential","hi":"वे पूंजी निर्माण तथा दीर्घकालिक विकास क्षमता बढ़ाती हैं"},"4":{"en":"They reduce productive capacity and constrain economic growth","hi":"वे उत्पादक क्षमता घटाती हैं तथा आर्थिक विकास को सीमित करती हैं"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – They enhance capital formation and long-term growth potential</b><br>Higher <b>domestic saving and investment rates</b> increase <b>capital formation</b>, finance new plant and machinery and thereby raise the economy's <b>long-term growth potential</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• In the <b>Harrod-Domar</b> framework, the growth rate depends on the <b>saving rate</b> and the capital-output ratio.<br>• After 1991, India's <b>gross domestic saving rate</b> and <b>investment rate</b> rose substantially, supporting higher GDP growth.<br>• Savings provide funds for investment without relying entirely on <b>foreign capital</b>, reducing external vulnerability.<br>• <b>Financial sector reforms, banking expansion and pension and insurance growth</b> helped mobilise household savings.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – वे पूंजी निर्माण तथा दीर्घकालिक विकास क्षमता बढ़ाती हैं</b><br>उच्च <b>घरेलू बचत तथा निवेश दरें</b> <b>पूंजी निर्माण</b> बढ़ाती हैं, नए संयंत्र एवं मशीनरी का वित्तपोषण करती हैं और इससे अर्थव्यवस्था की <b>दीर्घकालिक विकास क्षमता</b> बढ़ती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>हैरोड-डोमर</b> ढाँचे में वृद्धि दर <b>बचत दर</b> तथा पूंजी-उत्पाद अनुपात पर निर्भर करती है।<br>• 1991 के बाद भारत की <b>सकल घरेलू बचत दर</b> तथा <b>निवेश दर</b> में उल्लेखनीय वृद्धि हुई, जिससे उच्च जीडीपी वृद्धि को सहारा मिला।<br>• बचतें पूर्णतः <b>विदेशी पूंजी</b> पर निर्भर रहने के बिना निवेश के लिए निधि उपलब्ध कराती हैं, जिससे बाह्य संवेदनशीलता घटती है।<br>• <b>वित्तीय क्षेत्र सुधार, बैंकिंग विस्तार तथा पेंशन एवं बीमा वृद्धि</b> ने घरेलू बचत जुटाने में सहायता की।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000071626","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"What is the primary objective of introducing risk-based inspection systems? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"जोखिम आधारित निरीक्षण प्रणाली शुरू करने का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Focus inspections on higher-risk entities while reducing unnecessary inspections","hi":"अनावश्यक निरीक्षण घटाते हुए उच्च जोखिम वाली संस्थाओं पर निरीक्षण केंद्रित करना"},"2":{"en":"Focus risk-based inspections equally on all business entities","hi":"जोखिम आधारित निरीक्षण सभी व्यावसायिक संस्थाओं पर समान रूप से केंद्रित करना"},"3":{"en":"Focus risk-based inspections on increasing the frequency of inspections","hi":"जोखिम आधारित निरीक्षण निरीक्षणों की आवृत्ति बढ़ाने पर केंद्रित करना"},"4":{"en":"Focus risk-based inspections on replacing digital governance systems","hi":"जोखिम आधारित निरीक्षण डिजिटल शासन प्रणालियों को बदलने पर केंद्रित करना"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Focus inspections on higher-risk entities while reducing unnecessary inspections</b><br><b>Risk-based inspection</b> uses data to identify <b>high-risk entities</b> and focuses regulatory checks on them, while <b>reducing unnecessary inspections</b> of low-risk units.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Such systems are part of the <b>ease of doing business</b> reforms and are promoted under the <b>Business Reforms Action Plan</b>.<br>• They reduce the <b>compliance burden</b> and scope for <b>inspector discretion and harassment</b>, using criteria such as past compliance record and risk category.<br>• They are supported by <b>randomised and computerised allocation of inspectors</b> and digital reporting of inspections.<br>• Regulatory bodies such as <b>SEBI, RBI, FSSAI and pollution control boards</b> increasingly use risk-based supervision.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – अनावश्यक निरीक्षण घटाते हुए उच्च जोखिम वाली संस्थाओं पर निरीक्षण केंद्रित करना</b><br><b>जोखिम आधारित निरीक्षण</b> आँकड़ों का उपयोग <b>उच्च जोखिम वाली संस्थाओं</b> की पहचान करने तथा उन पर नियामक जाँच केंद्रित करने के लिए करता है, साथ ही कम जोखिम वाली इकाइयों के <b>अनावश्यक निरीक्षण घटाता</b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ऐसी प्रणालियाँ <b>व्यापार सुगमता</b> सुधारों का भाग हैं और <b>व्यापार सुधार कार्य योजना</b> के अंतर्गत बढ़ावा दी जाती हैं।<br>• ये <b>अनुपालन बोझ</b> तथा <b>निरीक्षक के विवेक एवं उत्पीड़न</b> की संभावना घटाती हैं और पूर्व अनुपालन रिकॉर्ड तथा जोखिम श्रेणी जैसे मानकों का उपयोग करती हैं।<br>• इन्हें <b>निरीक्षकों के यादृच्छिक एवं कंप्यूटरीकृत आवंटन</b> तथा निरीक्षणों की डिजिटल रिपोर्टिंग का समर्थन प्राप्त है।<br>• <b>सेबी, आरबीआई, एफएसएसएआई तथा प्रदूषण नियंत्रण बोर्ड</b> जैसे नियामक जोखिम आधारित पर्यवेक्षण अपना रहे हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000071627","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Reports and Indices (Current)","question":{"en":"According to the World Happiness Report 2026, most countries whose life-evaluation scores increased by at least one point between the 2006-2010 base period and 2023-2025 were located in which region? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"विश्व प्रसन्नता रिपोर्ट 2026 के अनुसार, जिन देशों के जीवन मूल्यांकन अंक 2006-2010 की आधार अवधि तथा 2023-2025 के बीच कम से कम एक अंक बढ़े, वे अधिकांशतः किस क्षेत्र में स्थित थे? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Central and Eastern Europe","hi":"मध्य तथा पूर्वी यूरोप"},"2":{"en":"Sub-Saharan Africa","hi":"उप-सहारा अफ्रीका"},"3":{"en":"Western and Northern Europe","hi":"पश्चिमी तथा उत्तरी यूरोप"},"4":{"en":"South and Central America","hi":"दक्षिण तथा मध्य अमेरिका"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Central and Eastern Europe</b><br>According to the <b>World Happiness Report 2026</b>, most countries whose <b>life-evaluation scores rose by at least one point</b> since the <b>2006-2010</b> base period were located in <b>Central and Eastern Europe</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Countries in this region have seen income growth, improved public services and rising social trust after their transition economies reformed.<br>• The report uses the <b>Cantril ladder</b> to measure life evaluation on a scale of 0 to 10.<br>• It also notes that some countries in <b>Sub-Saharan Africa and South Asia</b> recorded declines in life evaluation over the same period.<br>• The report is published by the <b>Wellbeing Research Centre, University of Oxford</b>, with Gallup and the UN SDSN, around <b>20 March</b> each year.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – मध्य तथा पूर्वी यूरोप</b><br><b>विश्व प्रसन्नता रिपोर्ट 2026</b> के अनुसार, जिन देशों के <b>जीवन मूल्यांकन अंक</b> <b>2006-2010</b> की आधार अवधि से <b>कम से कम एक अंक</b> बढ़े, वे अधिकांशतः <b>मध्य तथा पूर्वी यूरोप</b> में स्थित थे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इस क्षेत्र के देशों ने अपनी संक्रमणकालीन अर्थव्यवस्थाओं में सुधार के बाद आय वृद्धि, बेहतर सार्वजनिक सेवाएँ तथा बढ़ता सामाजिक विश्वास देखा है।<br>• रिपोर्ट जीवन मूल्यांकन मापने के लिए <b>कैंट्रिल लैडर</b> का उपयोग करती है, जिसका पैमाना 0 से 10 है।<br>• यह यह भी बताती है कि <b>उप-सहारा अफ्रीका तथा दक्षिण एशिया</b> के कुछ देशों में इसी अवधि में जीवन मूल्यांकन घटा है।<br>• रिपोर्ट <b>ऑक्सफोर्ड विश्वविद्यालय के वेलबीइंग रिसर्च सेंटर</b> द्वारा गैलप तथा संयुक्त राष्ट्र SDSN के साथ प्रतिवर्ष <b>20 मार्च</b> के आसपास प्रकाशित होती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000071628","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Reports and Indices (Current)","question":{"en":"The country rankings in the World Happiness Report are based on respondents' answers to which type of measure? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"विश्व प्रसन्नता रिपोर्ट में देशों की रैंकिंग उत्तरदाताओं के किस प्रकार के माप के उत्तरों पर आधारित होती है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Average life evaluation scores","hi":"औसत जीवन मूल्यांकन अंक"},"2":{"en":"Human Development Index scores","hi":"मानव विकास सूचकांक अंक"},"3":{"en":"Happiness Quotient scores","hi":"प्रसन्नता भागफल अंक"},"4":{"en":"Gross domestic product growth rates","hi":"सकल घरेलू उत्पाद वृद्धि दरें"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Average life evaluation scores</b><br>The country rankings in the <b>World Happiness Report</b> are based on <b>average life evaluation scores</b> of respondents, measured through the <b>Cantril ladder</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• In the Cantril ladder, respondents rate their <b>present life on a scale of 0 to 10</b>, where 10 is the best possible life.<br>• These scores are then explained using six factors: <b>GDP per capita, social support, healthy life expectancy, freedom, generosity and perceptions of corruption</b>.<br>• The <b>Human Development Index</b> is published by <b>UNDP</b> and uses income, health and education indicators, not survey responses on life evaluation.<br>• The report is a partnership of the <b>University of Oxford Wellbeing Research Centre, Gallup and the UN SDSN</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – औसत जीवन मूल्यांकन अंक</b><br><b>विश्व प्रसन्नता रिपोर्ट</b> में देशों की रैंकिंग उत्तरदाताओं के <b>औसत जीवन मूल्यांकन अंकों</b> पर आधारित होती है, जो <b>कैंट्रिल लैडर</b> से मापे जाते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• कैंट्रिल लैडर में उत्तरदाता अपने <b>वर्तमान जीवन को 0 से 10 के पैमाने</b> पर आँकते हैं, जहाँ 10 सर्वोत्तम संभव जीवन है।<br>• इन अंकों की व्याख्या छह कारकों से की जाती है: <b>प्रति व्यक्ति जीडीपी, सामाजिक सहायता, स्वस्थ जीवन प्रत्याशा, स्वतंत्रता, उदारता तथा भ्रष्टाचार की धारणा</b>।<br>• <b>मानव विकास सूचकांक</b> <b>यूएनडीपी</b> प्रकाशित करता है और इसमें आय, स्वास्थ्य तथा शिक्षा के संकेतक प्रयोग होते हैं, जीवन मूल्यांकन पर सर्वेक्षण उत्तर नहीं।<br>• यह रिपोर्ट <b>ऑक्सफोर्ड विश्वविद्यालय के वेलबीइंग रिसर्च सेंटर, गैलप तथा संयुक्त राष्ट्र SDSN</b> की साझेदारी है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000071629","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Ecosystem","question":{"en":"A region experiences deforestation, soil erosion, altered river flow, and local climate shifts. Which conclusion reflects the most integrated ecosystem perspective? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी क्षेत्र में वनों की कटाई, मृदा अपरदन, नदी के प्रवाह में परिवर्तन तथा स्थानीय जलवायु में परिवर्तन होता है। कौन-सा निष्कर्ष सर्वाधिक समेकित पारितंत्र दृष्टिकोण को दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only the carbon cycle is affected.","hi":"केवल कार्बन चक्र प्रभावित होता है।"},"2":{"en":"Ecosystem degradation disrupts interconnected cycles.","hi":"पारितंत्र क्षरण परस्पर जुड़े चक्रों को बाधित करता है।"},"3":{"en":"Soil erosion occurs independently of biodiversity loss.","hi":"मृदा अपरदन जैव विविधता हानि से स्वतंत्र रूप से होता है।"},"4":{"en":"Abiotic components recover instantly after disturbance.","hi":"अजैविक घटक विक्षोभ के बाद तत्काल पुनःस्थापित हो जाते हैं।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Ecosystem degradation disrupts interconnected cycles.</b><br>Deforestation, soil erosion, changed river flow and local climate shifts together show that <b>ecosystem degradation disrupts interconnected cycles</b> such as the water, carbon and nutrient cycles.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Forests regulate the <b>hydrological cycle</b> by intercepting rainfall and maintaining infiltration, so their loss increases runoff and soil erosion.<br>• Erosion reduces <b>soil fertility and carbon storage</b>, while loss of vegetation affects <b>biodiversity and local rainfall</b>.<br>• The <b>ecosystem approach</b> studies these linkages as a whole rather than as isolated problems, which is the basis of <b>Integrated Watershed Management</b>.<br>• Abiotic components such as soil and water do <b>not</b> recover instantly; their restoration often takes decades.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पारितंत्र क्षरण परस्पर जुड़े चक्रों को बाधित करता है।</b><br>वनों की कटाई, मृदा अपरदन, नदी प्रवाह में परिवर्तन तथा स्थानीय जलवायु परिवर्तन मिलकर दर्शाते हैं कि <b>पारितंत्र क्षरण परस्पर जुड़े चक्रों</b> जैसे जल, कार्बन तथा पोषक चक्रों <b>को बाधित करता है</b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वन वर्षा को रोककर तथा अंतःस्रवण बनाए रखकर <b>जल-चक्र</b> का नियमन करते हैं, अतः उनके विनाश से अपवाह तथा मृदा अपरदन बढ़ता है।<br>• अपरदन से <b>मृदा उर्वरता तथा कार्बन भंडारण</b> घटता है, जबकि वनस्पति हानि <b>जैव विविधता तथा स्थानीय वर्षा</b> को प्रभावित करती है।<br>• <b>पारितंत्र उपागम</b> इन संबंधों का समग्र रूप से अध्ययन करता है, न कि पृथक समस्याओं के रूप में; यही <b>समेकित जलग्रह प्रबंधन</b> का आधार है।<br>• मृदा तथा जल जैसे अजैविक घटक <b>तत्काल</b> पुनःस्थापित नहीं होते; उनकी पुनर्स्थापना में प्रायः दशक लगते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000071630","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which of the following statements about the gharial is most accurate? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"घड़ियाल के बारे में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन सर्वाधिक सटीक है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Gharials are widespread across India.","hi":"घड़ियाल पूरे भारत में व्यापक रूप से पाए जाते हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Gharials are threatened mainly by a shortage of natural prey.","hi":"घड़ियाल मुख्यतः प्राकृतिक शिकार की कमी से संकटग्रस्त हैं।"},"3":{"en":"Gharial is endemic to India and highly threatened.","hi":"घड़ियाल भारत में स्थानिक तथा अत्यधिक संकटग्रस्त है।"},"4":{"en":"Gharials are commonly found in both freshwater and marine habitats.","hi":"घड़ियाल सामान्यतः ताजे जल तथा समुद्री दोनों आवासों में पाए जाते हैं।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Gharial is endemic to India and highly threatened.</b><br>The <b>gharial</b> is a <b>critically endangered</b> crocodilian found mainly in the <b>Chambal, Girwa, Son and Mahanadi</b> river systems of India and Nepal, with the bulk of the population in India.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The gharial is listed as <b>Critically Endangered</b> by the IUCN and is in <b>Schedule I</b> of the Wild Life (Protection) Act, 1972.<br>• Its main threats are <b>loss of riverine habitat, sand mining, fishing nets, pollution and river damming</b>, rather than shortage of prey.<br>• It is a <b>freshwater</b> species with a long, narrow snout adapted for catching fish, and is not found in marine habitats.<br>• Conservation efforts include the <b>National Chambal Sanctuary</b>, captive breeding at <b>Kukrail</b> and projects by the <b>Madras Crocodile Bank</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – घड़ियाल भारत में स्थानिक तथा अत्यधिक संकटग्रस्त है।</b><br><b>घड़ियाल</b> एक <b>गंभीर रूप से संकटग्रस्त</b> मगरमच्छ प्रजाति है, जो मुख्यतः भारत तथा नेपाल की <b>चंबल, गिरवा, सोन तथा महानदी</b> नदी प्रणालियों में पाई जाती है, और इसकी अधिकांश आबादी भारत में है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• घड़ियाल IUCN द्वारा <b>गंभीर रूप से संकटग्रस्त</b> सूचीबद्ध है और वन्यजीव (संरक्षण) अधिनियम, 1972 की <b>अनुसूची I</b> में है।<br>• इसके मुख्य संकट <b>नदी आवास की हानि, बालू खनन, मत्स्य जाल, प्रदूषण तथा नदी बाँध</b> हैं, शिकार की कमी नहीं।<br>• यह <b>ताजे जल</b> की प्रजाति है, जिसका लंबा पतला थूथन मछली पकड़ने के अनुकूल है; यह समुद्री आवास में नहीं पाई जाती।<br>• संरक्षण प्रयासों में <b>राष्ट्रीय चंबल अभयारण्य</b>, <b>कुकरैल</b> में बंदी प्रजनन तथा <b>मद्रास क्रोकोडाइल बैंक</b> की परियोजनाएँ शामिल हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000071631","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"When a number is divided by 3, it gives a remainder of 2. Additionally, when the resulting quotient is divided by 7, the remainder is 5. What will the remainder be when the original number is divided by 21? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"जब किसी संख्या को 3 से विभाजित किया जाता है, तो शेषफल 2 प्राप्त होता है। इसके अतिरिक्त, जब प्राप्त भागफल को 7 से विभाजित किया जाता है, तो शेषफल 5 होता है। मूल संख्या को 21 से विभाजित करने पर शेषफल क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"13"},"2":{"en":"17"},"3":{"en":"18"},"4":{"en":"19"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(N = 3q + 2\\) and \\(q = 7k + 5\\)<br>\\(N = 3(7k + 5) + 2 = 21k + 17\\)<br>Remainder on division by 21 = \\(\\boxed{17}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 17.</b>","hi":"\\(N = 3q + 2\\) और \\(q = 7k + 5\\)<br>\\(N = 3(7k + 5) + 2 = 21k + 17\\)<br>21 से भाग देने पर शेषफल = \\(\\boxed{17}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 17 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000071632","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A regular right pyramid has an equilateral triangular base with side length 8 cm and height 10 cm. Find the volume of the pyramid. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक सम लंब पिरामिड का आधार समबाहु त्रिभुज है जिसकी भुजा 8 cm और ऊँचाई 10 cm है। पिरामिड का आयतन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"56.37 cm³"},"2":{"en":"82.56 cm³"},"3":{"en":"92.37 cm³"},"4":{"en":"72.56 cm³"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"250\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 250 185\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M60 152H185L125 114Z\"/><path d=\"M123.3 40L60 152M123.3 40L185 152M123.3 40L125 114\"/><path d=\"M123.3 40V139.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M136 139.3V152M136 139.3H148\"/><circle cx=\"123.3\" cy=\"139.3\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"123.3\" cy=\"40\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"123\" y=\"34\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"123\" y=\"34\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"166\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"166\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"166\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"166\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"118\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">D</text><text x=\"118\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">D</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">8 cm</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">8 cm</text><text x=\"128\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">10 cm</text><text x=\"128\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">10 cm</text></g></svg><br>Area of an equilateral base = \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\times 8^2 = 16\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>Volume = \\(\\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{base area} \\times \\text{height}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{3} \\times 16\\sqrt{3} \\times 10 = \\frac{160\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{92.37}\\) cm³<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 92.37 cm³.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"250\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 250 185\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M60 152H185L125 114Z\"/><path d=\"M123.3 40L60 152M123.3 40L185 152M123.3 40L125 114\"/><path d=\"M123.3 40V139.3\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M136 139.3V152M136 139.3H148\"/><circle cx=\"123.3\" cy=\"139.3\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"123.3\" cy=\"40\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"123\" y=\"34\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"123\" y=\"34\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"166\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"166\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"166\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"190\" y=\"166\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"118\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">D</text><text x=\"118\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">D</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">8 cm</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">8 cm</text><text x=\"128\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">10 cm</text><text x=\"128\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">10 cm</text></g></svg><br>समबाहु आधार का क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\times 8^2 = 16\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>आयतन = \\(\\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{आधार क्षेत्रफल} \\times \\text{ऊँचाई}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{3} \\times 16\\sqrt{3} \\times 10 = \\frac{160\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{92.37}\\) cm³<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 92.37 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000071633","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Convert 20° to radians. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"20° को रेडियन में बदलिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"π/9"},"2":{"en":"5π/6"},"3":{"en":"π/6"},"4":{"en":"11π/6"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(20^\\circ = 20 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{180}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{\\pi}{9}}\\) radians<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): π/9.</b>","hi":"\\(20^\\circ = 20 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{180}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{\\pi}{9}}\\) रेडियन<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): π/9 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000071634","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If tanθ=3/4, then find secθ. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि tanθ=3/4 है, तो secθ ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4/3"},"2":{"en":"5/4"},"3":{"en":"5/3"},"4":{"en":"5/2"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sec^2\\theta = 1 + \\tan^2\\theta = 1 + \\frac{9}{16} = \\frac{25}{16}\\)<br>\\(\\sec\\theta = \\boxed{\\frac{5}{4}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 5/4.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sec^2\\theta = 1 + \\tan^2\\theta = 1 + \\frac{9}{16} = \\frac{25}{16}\\)<br>\\(\\sec\\theta = \\boxed{\\frac{5}{4}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 5/4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000071635","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"The variable x is inversely proportional to the square of y. If x = 45 when y = 3, find the value of x when y = 9. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"चर x, y के वर्ग का व्युत्क्रमानुपाती है। यदि y = 3 होने पर x = 45 है, तो y = 9 होने पर x का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10"},"2":{"en":"12"},"3":{"en":"6"},"4":{"en":"5"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(x = \\frac{k}{y^2}\\)<br>\\(45 = \\frac{k}{9} \\Rightarrow k = 405\\)<br>When \\(y = 9\\): \\(x = \\frac{405}{81} = \\boxed{5}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 5.</b>","hi":"\\(x = \\frac{k}{y^2}\\)<br>\\(45 = \\frac{k}{9} \\Rightarrow k = 405\\)<br>जब \\(y = 9\\): \\(x = \\frac{405}{81} = \\boxed{5}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000071636","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"The sum of seven consecutive natural numbers is K. If the next three natural numbers are also included, the new sum becomes K + 93. What is the largest of the original seven numbers? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सात क्रमागत प्राकृत संख्याओं का योग K है। यदि अगली तीन प्राकृत संख्याएँ भी शामिल कर ली जाएँ, तो नया योग K + 93 हो जाता है। मूल सात संख्याओं में सबसे बड़ी संख्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"31"},"2":{"en":"29"},"3":{"en":"34"},"4":{"en":"36"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let the seven numbers be \\(a, a+1, \\ldots, a+6\\), so the largest is \\(a + 6\\)<br>The next three are \\(a+7, a+8, a+9\\)<br>\\(a+7 + a+8 + a+9 = 93 \\Rightarrow 3a + 24 = 93 \\Rightarrow a = 23\\)<br>Largest = \\(23 + 6 = \\boxed{29}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 29.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए सात संख्याएँ \\(a, a+1, \\ldots, a+6\\) हैं, अतः सबसे बड़ी \\(a + 6\\) है<br>अगली तीन \\(a+7, a+8, a+9\\) हैं<br>\\(a+7 + a+8 + a+9 = 93 \\Rightarrow 3a + 24 = 93 \\Rightarrow a = 23\\)<br>सबसे बड़ी = \\(23 + 6 = \\boxed{29}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 29 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000071637","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"Find the annual rate of compound interest at which a sum of ₹8,000 becomes ₹9,261 in 3 years. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वह वार्षिक चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज दर ज्ञात कीजिए जिस पर ₹8,000 की राशि 3 वर्षों में ₹9,261 हो जाती है। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2%"},"2":{"en":"5%"},"3":{"en":"8%"},"4":{"en":"10%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(9261 = 8000\\left(1 + \\frac{r}{100}\\right)^3\\)<br>\\(\\left(1 + \\frac{r}{100}\\right)^3 = \\frac{9261}{8000} = \\left(\\frac{21}{20}\\right)^3\\)<br>\\(1 + \\frac{r}{100} = \\frac{21}{20} \\Rightarrow r = \\boxed{5}\\)%<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 5%.</b>","hi":"\\(9261 = 8000\\left(1 + \\frac{r}{100}\\right)^3\\)<br>\\(\\left(1 + \\frac{r}{100}\\right)^3 = \\frac{9261}{8000} = \\left(\\frac{21}{20}\\right)^3\\)<br>\\(1 + \\frac{r}{100} = \\frac{21}{20} \\Rightarrow r = \\boxed{5}\\)%<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 5% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000071638","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A square field of side 40 m has a 2 m wide path running inside it along the boundary. What is the ratio of the area of the path to the area of the remaining field? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"40 m भुजा वाले एक वर्गाकार मैदान के अंदर परिसीमा के साथ 2 m चौड़ा रास्ता है। रास्ते के क्षेत्रफल और शेष मैदान के क्षेत्रफल का अनुपात क्या है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"19:81"},"2":{"en":"21:79"},"3":{"en":"36:83"},"4":{"en":"44:51"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"270\" height=\"230\" viewBox=\"0 0 270 230\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M50 30H210V190H50Z M56 36H204V184H56Z\" fill=\"#e9e9e9\" fill-rule=\"evenodd\" stroke=\"none\"/><path d=\"M50 30H210V190H50Z\"/><path d=\"M56 36H204V184H56Z\"/><path d=\"M56 36H70M56 36V50\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"206\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">40 m</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"206\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">40 m</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">2 m</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">2 m</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">remaining field</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">remaining field</text></g></svg><br>Area of the field = \\(40^2 = 1600\\) m²<br>Remaining field = \\((40 - 4)^2 = 36^2 = 1296\\) m²<br>Path area = \\(1600 - 1296 = 304\\) m²<br>Ratio = \\(304 : 1296 = \\boxed{19:81}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 19:81.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"270\" height=\"230\" viewBox=\"0 0 270 230\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M50 30H210V190H50Z M56 36H204V184H56Z\" fill=\"#e9e9e9\" fill-rule=\"evenodd\" stroke=\"none\"/><path d=\"M50 30H210V190H50Z\"/><path d=\"M56 36H204V184H56Z\"/><path d=\"M56 36H70M56 36V50\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"206\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">40 m</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"206\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">40 m</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">2 m</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"50\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">2 m</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">remaining field</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"116\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">remaining field</text></g></svg><br>मैदान का क्षेत्रफल = \\(40^2 = 1600\\) m²<br>शेष मैदान = \\((40 - 4)^2 = 36^2 = 1296\\) m²<br>रास्ते का क्षेत्रफल = \\(1600 - 1296 = 304\\) m²<br>अनुपात = \\(304 : 1296 = \\boxed{19:81}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 19:81 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000071639","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"Points P and Q are on the same side of a tower. The angles of elevation are 30° and 45°. The distance between them is 56 m. Find the height of the tower. Use(√3 = 1.732) [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"बिंदु P और Q एक मीनार के एक ही ओर हैं। उन्नयन कोण 30° और 45° हैं। उनके बीच की दूरी 56 m है। मीनार की ऊँचाई ज्ञात कीजिए। (√3 = 1.732 लीजिए) [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"70.5 m"},"2":{"en":"70.2 m"},"3":{"en":"79.2 m"},"4":{"en":"76.5 m"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M20 140H230\"/><path d=\"M40 140V40H48V140\"/><path d=\"M40 40L135 140M40 40L207.5 140\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M40 40H48M48 40V48\"/><path d=\"M135 148H207.5M135 143V153M207.5 143V153\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"94\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">h</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"94\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">h</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">30°</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">30°</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">45°</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">45°</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">P</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">P</text><text x=\"213\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Q</text><text x=\"213\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Q</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">56 m</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">56 m</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{h}{\\tan 30^\\circ} - \\frac{h}{\\tan 45^\\circ} = 56\\)<br>\\(h(\\sqrt{3} - 1) = 56\\)<br>\\(h = \\frac{56}{0.732} = 76.5\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{76.5}\\) m<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 76.5 m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M20 140H230\"/><path d=\"M40 140V40H48V140\"/><path d=\"M40 40L135 140M40 40L207.5 140\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M40 40H48M48 40V48\"/><path d=\"M135 148H207.5M135 143V153M207.5 143V153\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"94\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">h</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"94\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">h</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">30°</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"60\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">30°</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">45°</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">45°</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">P</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">P</text><text x=\"213\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Q</text><text x=\"213\" y=\"135\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Q</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">56 m</text><text x=\"171\" y=\"172\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">56 m</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{h}{\\tan 30^\\circ} - \\frac{h}{\\tan 45^\\circ} = 56\\)<br>\\(h(\\sqrt{3} - 1) = 56\\)<br>\\(h = \\frac{56}{0.732} = 76.5\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{76.5}\\) m<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 76.5 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000071640","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Solve: \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4} - \\sqrt{3}}\\) [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"हल कीजिए: \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4} - \\sqrt{3}}\\) [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{2} - 2\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{3} - 2\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{2} + 2\\)"},"4":{"en":"0"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}} = \\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4} - \\sqrt{3}} = \\sqrt{4} + \\sqrt{3} = 2 + \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>Expression = \\((\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2}) - (2 + \\sqrt{3})\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\sqrt{2} - 2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\sqrt{2} - 2\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}} = \\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4} - \\sqrt{3}} = \\sqrt{4} + \\sqrt{3} = 2 + \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>व्यंजक = \\((\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2}) - (2 + \\sqrt{3})\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\sqrt{2} - 2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\sqrt{2} - 2\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000071641","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Find the value of \\(\\sqrt{13 - 2\\sqrt{42}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13 - 2\\sqrt{42}}}\\). [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{13 - 2\\sqrt{42}} - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{13 - 2\\sqrt{42}}}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(-2\\sqrt{6}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{6}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(-2\\sqrt{7}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{7}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{13 - 2\\sqrt{42}} = \\sqrt{7} - \\sqrt{6}\\) because \\((\\sqrt{7} - \\sqrt{6})^2 = 13 - 2\\sqrt{42}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7} - \\sqrt{6}} = \\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{6}\\)<br>Expression = \\((\\sqrt{7} - \\sqrt{6}) - (\\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{6})\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{-2\\sqrt{6}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(-2\\sqrt{6}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{13 - 2\\sqrt{42}} = \\sqrt{7} - \\sqrt{6}\\) क्योंकि \\((\\sqrt{7} - \\sqrt{6})^2 = 13 - 2\\sqrt{42}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{7} - \\sqrt{6}} = \\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{6}\\)<br>व्यंजक = \\((\\sqrt{7} - \\sqrt{6}) - (\\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{6})\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{-2\\sqrt{6}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(-2\\sqrt{6}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000071642","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A cubical block with side length 6 cm has a hemispherical cavity of diameter 2 cm removed from each of its faces. Calculate the approximate surface area of the resulting solid. (Use π = 22/7) [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"6 cm भुजा वाले एक घनाकार गुटके के प्रत्येक फलक से 2 cm व्यास का अर्धगोलाकार गड्ढा निकाला जाता है। परिणामी ठोस का अनुमानित पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। (π = 22/7 लीजिए) [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"357.12 cm²"},"2":{"en":"378.18 cm²"},"3":{"en":"256.95 cm²"},"4":{"en":"234.86 cm²"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"260\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 260 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M50 45H160V155H50Z\"/><path d=\"M95 17H205V127H95Z\"/><path d=\"M50 45L95 17M160 45L205 17M160 155L205 127\"/><path d=\"M93 100a12 12 0 1 0 24 0a12 12 0 1 0 -24 0\"/><path d=\"M93 100A12 6 0 0 1 117 100\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M93 100A12 6 0 0 0 117 100\"/><path d=\"M117 100H128\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"105\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">6 cm</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">6 cm</text><text x=\"136\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">r = 1</text><text x=\"136\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">r = 1</text></g></svg><br>Cube surface area = \\(6 \\times 36 = 216\\) cm², radius of each cavity = 1 cm<br>Six circular openings are removed = \\(6\\pi r^2 = 6 \\times \\frac{22}{7} = 18.86\\) cm²<br>Six hemispherical curved surfaces added = \\(6 \\times 2\\pi r^2 = 12 \\times \\frac{22}{7} = 37.71\\) cm²<br>Surface area = \\(216 - 18.86 + 37.71 = 234.85\\)<br>\\(\\approx \\boxed{234.86}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 234.86 cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"260\" height=\"190\" viewBox=\"0 0 260 190\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M50 45H160V155H50Z\"/><path d=\"M95 17H205V127H95Z\"/><path d=\"M50 45L95 17M160 45L205 17M160 155L205 127\"/><path d=\"M93 100a12 12 0 1 0 24 0a12 12 0 1 0 -24 0\"/><path d=\"M93 100A12 6 0 0 1 117 100\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M93 100A12 6 0 0 0 117 100\"/><path d=\"M117 100H128\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><circle cx=\"105\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"105\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">6 cm</text><text x=\"105\" y=\"176\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">6 cm</text><text x=\"136\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">r = 1</text><text x=\"136\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">r = 1</text></g></svg><br>घन का पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल = \\(6 \\times 36 = 216\\) cm², प्रत्येक गड्ढे की त्रिज्या = 1 cm<br>छह वृत्ताकार छिद्र हटाए जाते हैं = \\(6\\pi r^2 = 6 \\times \\frac{22}{7} = 18.86\\) cm²<br>छह अर्धगोलाकार वक्र पृष्ठ जोड़े जाते हैं = \\(6 \\times 2\\pi r^2 = 12 \\times \\frac{22}{7} = 37.71\\) cm²<br>पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल = \\(216 - 18.86 + 37.71 = 234.85\\)<br>\\(\\approx \\boxed{234.86}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 234.86 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000071643","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A chord of length 40 cm is at a distance of 21 cm from the center of a circle. What is the radius of the circle? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"40 cm लंबाई की एक जीवा वृत्त के केंद्र से 21 cm की दूरी पर है। वृत्त की त्रिज्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10.5 cm"},"2":{"en":"20 cm"},"3":{"en":"18.5 cm"},"4":{"en":"29 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"250\" height=\"205\" viewBox=\"0 0 250 205\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"95\" r=\"87\"/><path d=\"M60 158H180\"/><path d=\"M120 95V158\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M120 95L180 158\"/><path d=\"M120 150H128V158\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"95\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"114\" y=\"91\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">O</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"91\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">O</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">21</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">21</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">20</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">20</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">20</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">20</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">29</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">29</text></g></svg><br>Half chord = \\(\\frac{40}{2} = 20\\) cm<br>Radius = \\(\\sqrt{21^2 + 20^2} = \\sqrt{441 + 400}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{29}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 29 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"250\" height=\"205\" viewBox=\"0 0 250 205\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"95\" r=\"87\"/><path d=\"M60 158H180\"/><path d=\"M120 95V158\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M120 95L180 158\"/><path d=\"M120 150H128V158\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"95\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"114\" y=\"91\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">O</text><text x=\"114\" y=\"91\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">O</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">21</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"130\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">21</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">20</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">20</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">20</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">20</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">29</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"138\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">29</text></g></svg><br>जीवा का आधा = \\(\\frac{40}{2} = 20\\) cm<br>त्रिज्या = \\(\\sqrt{21^2 + 20^2} = \\sqrt{441 + 400}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{29}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 29 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000071644","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"The decimal expansion of a real number is eventually periodic if and only if the number is: [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी वास्तविक संख्या का दशमलव प्रसार अंततः आवर्ती होता है यदि और केवल यदि वह संख्या है: [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Irrational","hi":"अपरिमेय"},"2":{"en":"Algebraic","hi":"बीजीय"},"3":{"en":"Rational","hi":"परिमेय"},"4":{"en":"Transcendental","hi":"अविभाज्य (transcendental)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"A rational number always has a terminating or eventually repeating decimal expansion<br>Conversely, every terminating or eventually repeating decimal can be written as a fraction<br>So the decimal expansion is eventually periodic exactly for \\(\\boxed{\\text{Rational}}\\) numbers<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Rational.</b>","hi":"परिमेय संख्या का दशमलव प्रसार सदैव सांत या अंततः आवर्ती होता है<br>इसके विपरीत, हर सांत या अंततः आवर्ती दशमलव को भिन्न के रूप में लिखा जा सकता है<br>अतः दशमलव प्रसार अंततः आवर्ती ठीक \\(\\boxed{\\text{परिमेय}}\\) संख्याओं के लिए होता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): परिमेय है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000071645","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"The side of a square is increased by 4 cm, causing its area to increase by 80 cm². What was the original side length? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक वर्ग की भुजा 4 cm बढ़ा दी जाती है, जिससे उसका क्षेत्रफल 80 cm² बढ़ जाता है। मूल भुजा की लंबाई क्या थी? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 cm"},"2":{"en":"2 cm"},"3":{"en":"4 cm"},"4":{"en":"8 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let the side be \\(a\\).<br>\\((a + 4)^2 - a^2 = 80\\)<br>\\(8a + 16 = 80 \\Rightarrow 8a = 64\\)<br>\\(a = \\boxed{8}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 8 cm.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए भुजा \\(a\\) है।<br>\\((a + 4)^2 - a^2 = 80\\)<br>\\(8a + 16 = 80 \\Rightarrow 8a = 64\\)<br>\\(a = \\boxed{8}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 8 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000071646","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A trader invested ₹8,40,000. One-third was invested for 12 years, one-fourth for 10 years, and the remainder for 8 years. All investments earned 10% per annum simple interest. Find the total interest. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक व्यापारी ने ₹8,40,000 निवेश किए। एक-तिहाई 12 वर्षों के लिए, एक-चौथाई 10 वर्षों के लिए और शेष 8 वर्षों के लिए निवेश किया गया। सभी निवेशों पर 10% वार्षिक साधारण ब्याज मिला। कुल ब्याज ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹8,00,000"},"2":{"en":"₹8,29,000"},"3":{"en":"₹8,26,000"},"4":{"en":"₹8,20,000"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"One-third = ₹2,80,000 for 12 years: interest = \\(\\frac{280000 \\times 10 \\times 12}{100} = 336000\\)<br>One-fourth = ₹2,10,000 for 10 years: interest = \\(\\frac{210000 \\times 10 \\times 10}{100} = 210000\\)<br>Remainder = ₹3,50,000 for 8 years: interest = \\(\\frac{350000 \\times 10 \\times 8}{100} = 280000\\)<br>Total = \\(336000 + 210000 + 280000 = \\boxed{826000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): ₹8,26,000.</b>","hi":"एक-तिहाई = ₹2,80,000, 12 वर्ष: ब्याज = \\(\\frac{280000 \\times 10 \\times 12}{100} = 336000\\)<br>एक-चौथाई = ₹2,10,000, 10 वर्ष: ब्याज = \\(\\frac{210000 \\times 10 \\times 10}{100} = 210000\\)<br>शेष = ₹3,50,000, 8 वर्ष: ब्याज = \\(\\frac{350000 \\times 10 \\times 8}{100} = 280000\\)<br>कुल = \\(336000 + 210000 + 280000 = \\boxed{826000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): ₹8,26,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000071647","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"In a chemistry lab, there are two glass beakers labeled as X and Y. X is filled with a certain volume of chemical 'M' while Y is filled with an equal volume of chemical 'N'. It is known that 'M' and 'N' do not react with one another instantly to form any other compounds. Netra transfers \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) of the content of X to Y, at first. She then transfers \\(\\frac{7}{10}\\) of the content of Y to X. Finally, she transfers \\(\\frac{4}{5}\\) of the content of X to Y. All these transfers are consecutive. Find the ratio of M to N (by volume) in Y, after the final transfer. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक रसायन प्रयोगशाला में X और Y नामक दो काँच के बीकर हैं। X में रसायन 'M' की एक निश्चित मात्रा भरी है जबकि Y में रसायन 'N' की उतनी ही मात्रा भरी है। यह ज्ञात है कि 'M' और 'N' तुरंत एक-दूसरे के साथ अभिक्रिया करके कोई अन्य यौगिक नहीं बनाते। नेत्रा सबसे पहले X की सामग्री का \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) भाग Y में स्थानांतरित करती है। फिर वह Y की सामग्री का \\(\\frac{7}{10}\\) भाग X में स्थानांतरित करती है। अंत में, वह X की सामग्री का \\(\\frac{4}{5}\\) भाग Y में स्थानांतरित करती है। ये सभी स्थानांतरण क्रमागत हैं। अंतिम स्थानांतरण के बाद Y में M और N का अनुपात (आयतन के अनुसार) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"17:14"},"2":{"en":"23:27"},"3":{"en":"41:49"},"4":{"en":"83:86"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let X hold 10 M and Y hold 10 N.<br>Step 1 – move \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) of X: X = (5 M), Y = (5 M + 10 N)<br>Step 2 – move \\(\\frac{7}{10}\\) of Y: 3.5 M and 7 N go to X, Y keeps 1.5 M + 3 N; X = 8.5 M + 7 N<br>Step 3 – move \\(\\frac{4}{5}\\) of X: 6.8 M + 5.6 N go to Y<br>Y now has \\(1.5 + 6.8 = 8.3\\) M and \\(3 + 5.6 = 8.6\\) N<br>Ratio = \\(8.3 : 8.6 = \\boxed{83:86}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 83:86.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए X में 10 M और Y में 10 N हैं।<br>चरण 1 – X का \\(\\frac{1}{2}\\) स्थानांतरित: X = (5 M), Y = (5 M + 10 N)<br>चरण 2 – Y का \\(\\frac{7}{10}\\) स्थानांतरित: 3.5 M और 7 N X में जाते हैं, Y में 1.5 M + 3 N बचते हैं; X = 8.5 M + 7 N<br>चरण 3 – X का \\(\\frac{4}{5}\\) स्थानांतरित: 6.8 M + 5.6 N Y में जाते हैं<br>अब Y में \\(1.5 + 6.8 = 8.3\\) M और \\(3 + 5.6 = 8.6\\) N हैं<br>अनुपात = \\(8.3 : 8.6 = \\boxed{83:86}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 83:86 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000071648","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"In a right-angled triangle ABC right-angled at C, what is the value of tanA · tanB? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"C पर समकोण वाले एक समकोण त्रिभुज ABC में, tanA · tanB का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"-1"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"230\" height=\"180\" viewBox=\"0 0 230 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M60 55V145H180Z\"/><path d=\"M60 133H72V145\"/><path d=\"M60 71A16 16 0 0 1 74 62\"/><path d=\"M165 145A16 16 0 0 0 171 132\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"186\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"186\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"84\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">tan A · tan B = ?</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"84\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">tan A · tan B = ?</text></g></svg><br>\\(A + B = 90^\\circ \\Rightarrow \\tan B = \\cot A\\)<br>\\(\\tan A \\cdot \\tan B = \\tan A \\cdot \\cot A\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"230\" height=\"180\" viewBox=\"0 0 230 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M60 55V145H180Z\"/><path d=\"M60 133H72V145\"/><path d=\"M60 71A16 16 0 0 1 74 62\"/><path d=\"M165 145A16 16 0 0 0 171 132\"/><text x=\"52\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"186\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"186\" y=\"152\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"46\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"84\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">tan A · tan B = ?</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"84\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">tan A · tan B = ?</text></g></svg><br>\\(A + B = 90^\\circ \\Rightarrow \\tan B = \\cot A\\)<br>\\(\\tan A \\cdot \\tan B = \\tan A \\cdot \\cot A\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000071649","section":"MATH","topic":"Progression","question":{"en":"The angles of a quadrilateral are in arithmetic progression. If the smallest angle measures 15°, find the largest angle in degrees. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक चतुर्भुज के कोण समांतर श्रेढ़ी में हैं। यदि सबसे छोटा कोण 15° है, तो सबसे बड़ा कोण डिग्री में ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"175°"},"2":{"en":"155°"},"3":{"en":"165°"},"4":{"en":"145°"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Angles: \\(15, 15+d, 15+2d, 15+3d\\)<br>Sum = \\(60 + 6d = 360 \\Rightarrow d = 50\\)<br>Largest = \\(15 + 3 \\times 50 = \\boxed{165^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 165°.</b>","hi":"कोण: \\(15, 15+d, 15+2d, 15+3d\\)<br>योग = \\(60 + 6d = 360 \\Rightarrow d = 50\\)<br>सबसे बड़ा = \\(15 + 3 \\times 50 = \\boxed{165^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 165° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000071650","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Evaluate: cosec 31° – sec 59° [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मान ज्ञात कीजिए: cosec 31° – sec 59° [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"−1"},"4":{"en":"0"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(31^\\circ + 59^\\circ = 90^\\circ \\Rightarrow \\sec 59^\\circ = \\sec(90^\\circ - 31^\\circ) = \\text{cosec}\\,31^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\text{cosec}\\,31^\\circ - \\text{cosec}\\,31^\\circ = \\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 0.</b>","hi":"\\(31^\\circ + 59^\\circ = 90^\\circ \\Rightarrow \\sec 59^\\circ = \\sec(90^\\circ - 31^\\circ) = \\text{cosec}\\,31^\\circ\\)<br>\\(\\text{cosec}\\,31^\\circ - \\text{cosec}\\,31^\\circ = \\boxed{0}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 0 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000071651","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If (x + y)²= 121 and (x - y)² = 9, what is the exact numerical value of the product xy? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि (x + y)²= 121 और (x - y)² = 9 है, तो गुणनफल xy का ठीक संख्यात्मक मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"14"},"2":{"en":"56"},"3":{"en":"130"},"4":{"en":"28"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\((x + y)^2 - (x - y)^2 = 4xy\\)<br>\\(121 - 9 = 4xy \\Rightarrow 4xy = 112\\)<br>\\(xy = \\boxed{28}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 28.</b>","hi":"\\((x + y)^2 - (x - y)^2 = 4xy\\)<br>\\(121 - 9 = 4xy \\Rightarrow 4xy = 112\\)<br>\\(xy = \\boxed{28}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 28 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000071652","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"From an external point T, two tangents TP and TQ are drawn to a circle. A third tangent line is drawn intersecting TP at point A and TQ at point B such that it touches the circle at point M. If the perimeter of ΔTAB is 24 cm, what is the length of the tangent segment TP? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी बाह्य बिंदु T से एक वृत्त पर दो स्पर्श रेखाएँ TP और TQ खींची जाती हैं। एक तीसरी स्पर्श रेखा खींची जाती है जो TP को बिंदु A पर और TQ को बिंदु B पर इस प्रकार काटती है कि वह वृत्त को बिंदु M पर स्पर्श करती है। यदि ΔTAB का परिमाप 24 cm है, तो स्पर्श रेखाखंड TP की लंबाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6 cm"},"2":{"en":"9 cm"},"3":{"en":"12 cm"},"4":{"en":"16 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"180\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"135\" cy=\"100\" r=\"52\"/><path d=\"M35 100L107 60M35 100L107 140\"/><path d=\"M81 76.7V123.3\"/><circle cx=\"135\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"81\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">T</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">T</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"56\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">P</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"56\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">P</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Q</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Q</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"64\" y=\"94\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">M</text><text x=\"64\" y=\"94\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">M</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">O</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">O</text></g></svg><br>Tangents from an external point are equal: \\(AP = AM\\) and \\(BQ = BM\\)<br>Perimeter of ΔTAB = \\(TA + AB + BT = TA + AM + MB + BT = TP + TQ\\)<br>\\(2TP = 24\\)<br>\\(TP = \\boxed{12}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 12 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"240\" height=\"180\" viewBox=\"0 0 240 180\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"135\" cy=\"100\" r=\"52\"/><path d=\"M35 100L107 60M35 100L107 140\"/><path d=\"M81 76.7V123.3\"/><circle cx=\"135\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"81\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">T</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">T</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"56\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">P</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"56\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">P</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">Q</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"146\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">Q</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"72\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"134\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"64\" y=\"94\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">M</text><text x=\"64\" y=\"94\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">M</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">O</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">O</text></g></svg><br>बाह्य बिंदु से खींची स्पर्श रेखाएँ बराबर होती हैं: \\(AP = AM\\) और \\(BQ = BM\\)<br>ΔTAB का परिमाप = \\(TA + AB + BT = TA + AM + MB + BT = TP + TQ\\)<br>\\(2TP = 24\\)<br>\\(TP = \\boxed{12}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 12 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000071653","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In ΔABC, AB = 15 units, AC = 12 units, and BC = 18 units. A point D lies on BC such that BD:DC = 2:1. A line through D parallel to AB meets AC at E. Find the length of AE. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"ΔABC में, AB = 15 इकाई, AC = 12 इकाई और BC = 18 इकाई है। बिंदु D, BC पर इस प्रकार स्थित है कि BD:DC = 2:1 है। D से होकर AB के समांतर खींची गई रेखा AC को E पर मिलती है। AE की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2 units","hi":"2 इकाई"},"2":{"en":"4 units","hi":"4 इकाई"},"3":{"en":"6 units","hi":"6 इकाई"},"4":{"en":"8 units","hi":"8 इकाई"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"280\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 185\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M50 152H235L162 51Z\"/><path d=\"M172 152L209 117\"/><text x=\"162\" y=\"44\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"162\" y=\"44\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"241\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"241\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">D</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">D</text><text x=\"213\" y=\"113\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">E</text><text x=\"213\" y=\"113\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">E</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">15</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">15</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">12</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">12</text><text x=\"106\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">18</text><text x=\"106\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">18</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{CD}{CB} = \\frac{1}{3}\\) and \\(DE \\parallel AB\\), so \\(\\frac{CE}{CA} = \\frac{CD}{CB} = \\frac{1}{3}\\)<br>\\(CE = \\frac{12}{3} = 4\\) units<br>\\(AE = 12 - 4 = \\boxed{8}\\) units<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 8 units.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"280\" height=\"185\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 185\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M50 152H235L162 51Z\"/><path d=\"M172 152L209 117\"/><text x=\"162\" y=\"44\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A</text><text x=\"162\" y=\"44\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B</text><text x=\"241\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C</text><text x=\"241\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">D</text><text x=\"166\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">D</text><text x=\"213\" y=\"113\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">E</text><text x=\"213\" y=\"113\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">E</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">15</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"96\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">15</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">12</text><text x=\"196\" y=\"80\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">12</text><text x=\"106\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">18</text><text x=\"106\" y=\"168\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">18</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{CD}{CB} = \\frac{1}{3}\\) और \\(DE \\parallel AB\\), अतः \\(\\frac{CE}{CA} = \\frac{CD}{CB} = \\frac{1}{3}\\)<br>\\(CE = \\frac{12}{3} = 4\\) इकाई<br>\\(AE = 12 - 4 = \\boxed{8}\\) इकाई<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 8 इकाई है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000071654","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two distinct coplanar circles can have exactly two common tangents in which of the following cases? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से किस स्थिति में दो भिन्न समतलीय वृत्तों की ठीक दो उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाएँ हो सकती हैं? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The circles are completely separate from each other.","hi":"वृत्त एक-दूसरे से पूर्णतः अलग हैं।"},"2":{"en":"The circles touch each other externally.","hi":"वृत्त एक-दूसरे को बाह्य रूप से स्पर्श करते हैं।"},"3":{"en":"The circles intersect at two distinct points.","hi":"वृत्त दो भिन्न बिंदुओं पर प्रतिच्छेद करते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"One circle lies completely inside the other without touching it.","hi":"एक वृत्त दूसरे के पूर्णतः भीतर है और उसे स्पर्श नहीं करता।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"250\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 250 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"95\" cy=\"100\" r=\"55\"/><circle cx=\"155\" cy=\"100\" r=\"55\"/><path d=\"M25 45H225M25 155H225\"/><circle cx=\"95\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"155\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"125\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">2 common tangents</text><text x=\"125\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">2 common tangents</text></g></svg><br>Two circles with two common tangents intersect at two points (in the second case they have 3, in the first 4, and in the fourth none)<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{The circles intersect at two distinct points}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): The circles intersect at two distinct points..</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"250\" height=\"200\" viewBox=\"0 0 250 200\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><circle cx=\"95\" cy=\"100\" r=\"55\"/><circle cx=\"155\" cy=\"100\" r=\"55\"/><path d=\"M25 45H225M25 155H225\"/><circle cx=\"95\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"155\" cy=\"100\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"125\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">2 common tangents</text><text x=\"125\" y=\"186\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">2 common tangents</text></g></svg><br>दो उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाएँ तब होती हैं जब वृत्त दो बिंदुओं पर प्रतिच्छेद करते हैं (दूसरी स्थिति में 3, पहली में 4 और चौथी में कोई नहीं)<br>\\(\\boxed{\\text{वृत्त दो भिन्न बिंदुओं पर प्रतिच्छेद करते हैं}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): वृत्त दो भिन्न बिंदुओं पर प्रतिच्छेद करते हैं। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000071655","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A and B together can complete a work in 10 days, B and C together in 15 days and C and A together in 20 days. D is three times as efficient as C. All four work together for 3 days. Then A and C work together for 5 days. Finally B and D complete the remaining work. If ₹30,000 is divided according to actual work done, what is B's share? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"A और B मिलकर एक कार्य 10 दिनों में, B और C मिलकर 15 दिनों में तथा C और A मिलकर 20 दिनों में पूरा कर सकते हैं। D, C से तीन गुना कुशल है। चारों मिलकर 3 दिन कार्य करते हैं। फिर A और C मिलकर 5 दिन कार्य करते हैं। अंत में B और D शेष कार्य पूरा करते हैं। यदि ₹30,000 वास्तविक किए गए कार्य के अनुसार बाँटे जाएँ, तो B का हिस्सा क्या है? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹12,000"},"2":{"en":"₹12,600"},"3":{"en":"₹13,200"},"4":{"en":"₹13,800"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Work = 60 units<br>\\(A + B = 6\\), \\(B + C = 4\\), \\(C + A = 3\\) \\(\\Rightarrow A + B + C = 6.5\\)<br>\\(A = 2.5\\), \\(B = 3.5\\), \\(C = 0.5\\), and \\(D = 3C = 1.5\\)<br>Work done: by B in first 3 days with A, C, D = \\(3.5 \\times 3 = 10.5\\)<br>Remaining work = \\(60 - 3(8) - 5(3) = 21\\) units; B's rate with D = 5, so B does \\(21 \\times \\frac{3.5}{5} = 14.7\\)<br>B's total = \\(10.5 + 14.7 = 25.2\\) units<br>B's share = \\(\\frac{25.2}{60} \\times 30000 = \\boxed{12600}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹12,600.</b>","hi":"कार्य = 60 इकाई<br>\\(A + B = 6\\), \\(B + C = 4\\), \\(C + A = 3\\) \\(\\Rightarrow A + B + C = 6.5\\)<br>\\(A = 2.5\\), \\(B = 3.5\\), \\(C = 0.5\\) और \\(D = 3C = 1.5\\)<br>किया गया कार्य: पहले 3 दिनों में B = \\(3.5 \\times 3 = 10.5\\)<br>शेष कार्य = \\(60 - 3(8) - 5(3) = 21\\) इकाई; D के साथ B की दर = 5, अतः B करता है \\(21 \\times \\frac{3.5}{5} = 14.7\\)<br>B का कुल कार्य = \\(10.5 + 14.7 = 25.2\\) इकाई<br>B का हिस्सा = \\(\\frac{25.2}{60} \\times 30000 = \\boxed{12600}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹12,600 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000071656","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Convert the below given indirect speech into direct speech appropriately:<br>The teacher said that the students had completed their assignments. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The teacher said, “The students are completing their assignments”."},"2":{"en":"The teacher said, “The students have completed their assignments”."},"3":{"en":"The teacher said, “The students complete their assignments”."},"4":{"en":"The teacher said, “The students will complete their assignments”."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past perfect reverses to present perfect in direct speech.</b><br>“Had completed” becomes “have completed.”<br>The subject “the students” remains unchanged.<br>The other options use present continuous, simple present or future tense.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The teacher said, “The students have completed their assignments”..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000071657","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Four parts of a sentence are given below in a jumbled order. When arranged correctly, they form a complete and meaningful sentence. While multiple combinations may appear grammatically correct, choose the one that best conveys the intended meaning as per the given options.<br>A) government welfare schemes<br>B) fail to avail<br>C) many beneficiaries<br>D) due to lack of awareness [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"B-C-A-D"},"2":{"en":"A-B-C-D"},"3":{"en":"C-B-A-D"},"4":{"en":"D-A-B-C"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: C-B-A-D</b><br>C supplies the subject: many beneficiaries.<br>B and A state what they fail to avail: government welfare schemes.<br>D gives the reason: lack of awareness.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): C-B-A-D.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000071658","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Four parts of a sentence are given below in a jumbled order. When arranged correctly, they form a complete and meaningful sentence. While multiple combinations may appear grammatically correct, choose the one that best conveys the intended meaning as per the given options.<br>A) of the National Education Policy<br>B) multilingual education<br>C) is a key feature<br>D) to enhance inclusivity [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"D-A-C-B"},"2":{"en":"A-B-C-D"},"3":{"en":"B-C-A-D"},"4":{"en":"C-A-B-D"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: B-C-A-D</b><br>B supplies the subject: multilingual education.<br>C and A identify it as a key feature of the National Education Policy.<br>D states its purpose: enhancing inclusivity.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): B-C-A-D.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000071659","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage below carefully and answer the questions that follow. Each question is based on the information provided in the passage. Ensure that you answer according to the content of the passage.<br><br>Climate change is beginning to impact Indian agriculture in visible ways. Rising temperatures, unpredictable rainfall, and extreme weather events are affecting crop yields across states like Punjab, Maharashtra, and West Bengal. Traditional farming calendars are becoming unreliable, forcing farmers to adapt by switching to shorter-duration or drought-resistant crops. Government initiatives like PM Fasal Bima Yojana provide crop insurance, but awareness and timely claim settlements remain a concern. Experts suggest combining modern weather forecasting with traditional knowledge to help farmers make informed decisions. Without timely interventions, food security and farmer livelihoods may face long-term risks.<br><br><br>How is climate change affecting Indian farmers? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Increasing profits"},"2":{"en":"Shortening work hours"},"3":{"en":"Reducing crop yields"},"4":{"en":"Making weather more predictable"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Rising temperatures, unpredictable rainfall and extreme weather affect crop yields.</b><br>Farmers face declining production and unreliable agricultural calendars.<br>Profits, work hours and predictability are not identified as benefits.<br>The passage instead warns of risks to livelihoods.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Reducing crop yields.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000071660","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage below carefully and answer the questions that follow. Each question is based on the information provided in the passage. Ensure that you answer according to the content of the passage.<br><br>Climate change is beginning to impact Indian agriculture in visible ways. Rising temperatures, unpredictable rainfall, and extreme weather events are affecting crop yields across states like Punjab, Maharashtra, and West Bengal. Traditional farming calendars are becoming unreliable, forcing farmers to adapt by switching to shorter-duration or drought-resistant crops. Government initiatives like PM Fasal Bima Yojana provide crop insurance, but awareness and timely claim settlements remain a concern. Experts suggest combining modern weather forecasting with traditional knowledge to help farmers make informed decisions. Without timely interventions, food security and farmer livelihoods may face long-term risks.<br><br><br>Which crops are farmers switching to? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"High-sugar crops"},"2":{"en":"Drought-resistant and short-duration crops"},"3":{"en":"Cotton and jute only"},"4":{"en":"Export-quality crops"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Farmers are switching to shorter-duration or drought-resistant crops.</b><br>These crops help them adapt to unreliable rainfall and extreme weather.<br>The passage does not mention high-sugar, cotton, jute or export-quality crops.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Drought-resistant and short-duration crops.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000071661","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage below carefully and answer the questions that follow. Each question is based on the information provided in the passage. Ensure that you answer according to the content of the passage.<br><br>Climate change is beginning to impact Indian agriculture in visible ways. Rising temperatures, unpredictable rainfall, and extreme weather events are affecting crop yields across states like Punjab, Maharashtra, and West Bengal. Traditional farming calendars are becoming unreliable, forcing farmers to adapt by switching to shorter-duration or drought-resistant crops. Government initiatives like PM Fasal Bima Yojana provide crop insurance, but awareness and timely claim settlements remain a concern. Experts suggest combining modern weather forecasting with traditional knowledge to help farmers make informed decisions. Without timely interventions, food security and farmer livelihoods may face long-term risks.<br><br><br>What is PM Fasal Bima Yojana? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Pension scheme"},"2":{"en":"Free loan waiver"},"3":{"en":"Educational policy"},"4":{"en":"Crop insurance initiative"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: PM Fasal Bima Yojana provides crop insurance.</b><br>It is intended to protect farmers against agricultural losses.<br>It is not a pension, loan waiver or educational policy.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Crop insurance initiative.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000071662","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage below carefully and answer the questions that follow. Each question is based on the information provided in the passage. Ensure that you answer according to the content of the passage.<br><br>Climate change is beginning to impact Indian agriculture in visible ways. Rising temperatures, unpredictable rainfall, and extreme weather events are affecting crop yields across states like Punjab, Maharashtra, and West Bengal. Traditional farming calendars are becoming unreliable, forcing farmers to adapt by switching to shorter-duration or drought-resistant crops. Government initiatives like PM Fasal Bima Yojana provide crop insurance, but awareness and timely claim settlements remain a concern. Experts suggest combining modern weather forecasting with traditional knowledge to help farmers make informed decisions. Without timely interventions, food security and farmer livelihoods may face long-term risks.<br><br><br>What is a challenge in PMFBY’s implementation? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Delay in claim settlement and awareness"},"2":{"en":"Too many online applications"},"3":{"en":"Lack of seeds"},"4":{"en":"Cold storage shortage"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Awareness and timely claim settlements remain concerns.</b><br>Farmers may not know about the scheme, and claims may be delayed.<br>Online applications, seeds and cold storage are not discussed.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Delay in claim settlement and awareness.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000071663","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage below carefully and answer the questions that follow. Each question is based on the information provided in the passage. Ensure that you answer according to the content of the passage.<br><br>Climate change is beginning to impact Indian agriculture in visible ways. Rising temperatures, unpredictable rainfall, and extreme weather events are affecting crop yields across states like Punjab, Maharashtra, and West Bengal. Traditional farming calendars are becoming unreliable, forcing farmers to adapt by switching to shorter-duration or drought-resistant crops. Government initiatives like PM Fasal Bima Yojana provide crop insurance, but awareness and timely claim settlements remain a concern. Experts suggest combining modern weather forecasting with traditional knowledge to help farmers make informed decisions. Without timely interventions, food security and farmer livelihoods may face long-term risks.<br><br><br>What combination is suggested for better adaptation? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Chemical pesticides + tractors"},"2":{"en":"Traditional knowledge + weather forecasting"},"3":{"en":"Foreign investments + subsidies"},"4":{"en":"Only mobile apps"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Experts suggest combining modern weather forecasting with traditional knowledge.</b><br>The combination helps farmers make informed decisions.<br>Pesticides, tractors, investments, subsidies and mobile-only solutions are not suggested.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Traditional knowledge + weather forecasting.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000071664","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom given below:<br>“Penny wise, pound foolish” [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Economical always"},"2":{"en":"Careful and rich"},"3":{"en":"Frugal yet careless in big matters"},"4":{"en":"Only saves big money"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Penny wise, pound foolish (छोटी बचत, बड़ी असावधानी) = careful in small matters but wasteful in large ones.</b><br>Example: “Skipping maintenance to save a little is penny wise, pound foolish.”<br>The idiom criticizes misplaced thrift, not consistent economy.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Frugal yet careless in big matters.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000071665","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Choose the correctly spelt word that best completes the sentence meaningfully.<br>The ___ of the meeting was clear: the new policy would improve employee morale. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"objctive"},"2":{"en":"objctve"},"3":{"en":"objective"},"4":{"en":"abjectve"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Objective (उद्देश्य) = goal or purpose.</b><br>The correct spelling is “objective.”<br><b>Objctive</b> omits “e”; <b>objctve</b> omits more letters.<br><b>Abjectve</b> uses “a” and omits “i.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): objective.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000071666","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>If he was knowing the answer (1)/ he would have responded (2)/ confidently in the interview (3)/ yesterday. (4) [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Know” is a stative verb and is not normally used in continuous form.</b><br>Part (1) should read “If he <b>had known</b> the answer” for an unreal past condition.<br>“Was knowing” is unidiomatic.<br>The other parts are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): (1).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000071667","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:<br>Her avowed neutrality (1)/ in the interdepartmental conflict (2)/ was belied by (3)/ her covert support to one faction. (4) [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The standard preposition after “support” is “for.”</b><br>Part (4) should read “her covert support <b>for</b> one faction.”<br>“Support to” is not the intended construction here.<br>The remaining parts are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): (4).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000071668","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the most appropriate option:<br>The consultant’s prognosis, though optimistic, failed to ___ the structural weaknesses evident in the model. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"diagnose"},"2":{"en":"address"},"3":{"en":"predict"},"4":{"en":"relieve"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Address (संबोधित करना) = deal with a problem.</b><br>The optimistic prognosis failed to address evident structural weaknesses.<br>“Diagnose” means identify, “predict” means forecast, and “relieve” means alleviate.<br>Only “address” conveys engaging with the weaknesses.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): address.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000071669","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Select the correct one-word substitution for:<br>A person who believes in or tries to bring about anarchy. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Patriot"},"2":{"en":"Anarchist"},"3":{"en":"Idealist"},"4":{"en":"Realist"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Anarchist (अराजकतावादी) = a person supporting or promoting anarchy.</b><br><b>Patriot (देशभक्त)</b> = one who loves their country<br><b>Idealist (आदर्शवादी)</b> = one guided by ideals<br><b>Realist (यथार्थवादी)</b> = one who accepts practical reality<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Anarchist.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000071670","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What is meant by the idiom “To jump the gun”? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To think things through before acting"},"2":{"en":"To delay taking action"},"3":{"en":"To complete a task without mistakes"},"4":{"en":"To act too soon or prematurely"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Jump the gun (समय से पहले कार्रवाई करना) = act prematurely.</b><br>Example: “Don’t jump the gun before the results are announced.”<br>Careful thought and delay are opposite ideas.<br>It does not mean completing a task perfectly.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): To act too soon or prematurely.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000071671","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What does the idiom “To cry wolf” mean? [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To ignore warnings or advice"},"2":{"en":"To express genuine concern"},"3":{"en":"To seek help in a time of need"},"4":{"en":"To raise a false alarm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Cry wolf (झूठा खतरा बताना) = raise a false alarm.</b><br>Example: “He has cried wolf so often that nobody believes him now.”<br>The idiom does not describe genuine concern or real need.<br>It concerns repeated false warnings.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): To raise a false alarm.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000071672","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Identify the correct spelling of the term which means the supreme legislative body in a country. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Parliamant"},"2":{"en":"Parliament"},"3":{"en":"Parlimant"},"4":{"en":"Parliment"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Parliament (संसद) = a country’s supreme legislative body.</b><br>The correct spelling is “parliament.”<br><b>Parliamant</b> replaces “e” with “a.”<br><b>Parlimant</b> and <b>parliment</b> omit “a.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Parliament.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000071673","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the underlined part of the sentence. If the sentence is already correct, select “No substitution required”.<br>He showed great interest in astronomy, an area that deeply <b>fascinates</b> him. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"fascinated"},"2":{"en":"was fascinating"},"3":{"en":"fascinates"},"4":{"en":"No substitution required"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Simple past “fascinated” aligns with the earlier past-time interest.</b><br>Correct wording: “an area that deeply <b>fascinated</b> him.”<br>“Was fascinating” changes the structure and aspect.<br>“Fascinates” retains a present-tense inconsistency in the keyed context.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): fascinated.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000071674","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the underlined part of the sentence. If the sentence is already correct, select “No substitution required”.<br>Had the research team accounted for seasonal variability, the conclusions drawn in the final report <b>would reflect</b> a more comprehensive understanding of climatic trends. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"would have reflected"},"2":{"en":"should reflect"},"3":{"en":"will reflect"},"4":{"en":"No substitution required"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Third conditional uses “if + past perfect” and “would have + past participle.”</b><br>The condition “Had … accounted” concerns an unreal past.<br>The result should be “would have reflected.”<br>“Should reflect” and “will reflect” do not express the counterfactual result.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): would have reflected.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000071675","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>The research team had already submitted the findings before the deadline. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The findings were submitted by the research team before the deadline."},"2":{"en":"The findings had been submitted by the research team before the deadline."},"3":{"en":"The findings were being submitted by the research team."},"4":{"en":"The findings were already submitting by the team."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past perfect passive = had been + past participle.</b><br>The object “the findings” becomes the subject.<br>“Had submitted” becomes “had been submitted,” and the agent and deadline are retained.<br>A and C use different aspects; D is ungrammatical.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The findings had been submitted by the research team before the deadline..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000071676","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>The developers have been updating the software regularly since its launch. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The software had been updated regularly since its launch."},"2":{"en":"The software is being updated regularly since its launch."},"3":{"en":"The software has been being updated regularly since its launch."},"4":{"en":"The software has been updated regularly since its launch."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Present perfect continuous passive = has/have been being + past participle.</b><br>The singular object “the software” becomes the subject.<br>“Has been being updated” retains the continuous activity since launch.<br>The other options change the tense or aspect.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): The software has been being updated regularly since its launch..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000071677","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"A sentence is provided in indirect speech. From the four given options, choose the one that most accurately conveys the sentence in its corresponding direct speech.<br>The judge remarked that it was regrettable that the accused had shown no remorse even after the gravity of the offense had been clearly established. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"“It is regrettable that you show no remorse despite your crime being proven,” said the judge."},"2":{"en":"“You haven't expressed any remorse even though we know how grave your offense is,” said the judge."},"3":{"en":"“How regrettable it is that even now, you do not regret your act,” the judge said."},"4":{"en":"“You should have shown remorse after your crime was proven,” remarked the judge."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Restore the present evaluation and direct address while retaining regret and established guilt.</b><br>A includes the judge’s regret, the accused’s lack of remorse and the proven crime.<br>B changes the opening evaluation, and C omits the established gravity.<br>D turns the remark into advice.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): “It is regrettable that you show no remorse despite your crime being proven,” said the judge..</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000071678","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful passage.<br>1. The request is routed to the IT department.<br>2. A ticket is raised by the user.<br>3. A technician is assigned based on availability.<br>4. The issue is resolved and marked closed. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-1-3-4"},"2":{"en":"2-3-1-4"},"3":{"en":"3-2-1-4"},"4":{"en":"1-2-3-4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-1-3-4</b><br>The user raises a ticket, and the request is routed to IT.<br>An available technician is assigned.<br>The issue is resolved and closed last.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2-1-3-4.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000071679","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the following sentences in correct order to make a meaningful sentence.<br>P. were finalized after months of inter-agency deliberations<br>Q. the national disaster response protocols<br>R. under the supervision of the central emergency council<br>S. to streamline rescue operations [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QPRS"},"2":{"en":"SPRQ"},"3":{"en":"QSRP"},"4":{"en":"QPSR"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QSRP</b><br>Q supplies the subject, and S states the protocols’ purpose.<br>R identifies the supervising council.<br>P completes the main predicate and deliberation period.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): QSRP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000071680","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitute for: “An indirect or subtle reference, typically critical in nature”. [SSC CGL 22/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Allusion"},"2":{"en":"Elusion"},"3":{"en":"Illusion"},"4":{"en":"Delusion"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Allusion (परोक्ष संकेत) = an indirect reference.</b><br><b>Elusion (बच निकलना)</b> = escape or avoidance<br><b>Illusion (भ्रम)</b> = false perception<br><b>Delusion (मतिभ्रम)</b> = firmly held false belief<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Allusion.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};